window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-08-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-08-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 08 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074481","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A says, “My father is the only son of B.” How is B related to A? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A कहता है, “मेरे पिता B के इकलौते पुत्र हैं।” B, A से किस प्रकार संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Grandfather","hi":"दादा"},"2":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"},"3":{"en":"Uncle","hi":"चाचा"},"4":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरा भाई"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"136\" y=\"8\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"136\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M146 50V62M146 82V104M146 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">B</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"76\">Father+</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"130\">A</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>B is the parent of A's father, so B is A's grandfather.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Grandfather.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"136\" y=\"8\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"136\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M146 50V62M146 82V104M146 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">B</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"76\">Father+</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"130\">A</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>B, A के पिता का पिता है, अतः B, A का दादा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): दादा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074482","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>21, 39, 119, ?, 707, 1411 [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रृंखला में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>21, 39, 119, ?, 707, 1411 [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"205"},"2":{"en":"215"},"3":{"en":"225"},"4":{"en":"235"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Alternate rule: ×2 − 3, ×3 + 2<br>21 × 2 − 3 = 39, 39 × 3 + 2 = 119, 119 × 2 − 3 = 235, 235 × 3 + 2 = 707, 707 × 2 − 3 = 1411 ✔<br>Missing number = 235<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 235.</b>","hi":"एकांतर नियम: ×2 − 3, ×3 + 2<br>21 × 2 − 3 = 39, 39 × 3 + 2 = 119, 119 × 2 − 3 = 235, 235 × 3 + 2 = 707, 707 × 2 − 3 = 1411 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = 235<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 235 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074483","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"The following symbols are used to represent family relationships:<br>1. P + Q indicates that P is the father of Q.<br>2. P × Q indicates that P is the mother of Q.<br>3. P ÷ Q indicates that P is the brother of Q.<br>4. P − Q indicates that P is the sister of Q.<br>Using the above coding pattern, determine the relationship of A with D in the given expression:<br>A + B − C × D [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पारिवारिक संबंधों को दर्शाने के लिए निम्नलिखित प्रतीकों का उपयोग किया जाता है:<br>1. P + Q का अर्थ है कि P, Q का पिता है।<br>2. P × Q का अर्थ है कि P, Q की माता है।<br>3. P ÷ Q का अर्थ है कि P, Q का भाई है।<br>4. P − Q का अर्थ है कि P, Q की बहन है।<br>उपरोक्त कोडिंग पैटर्न का उपयोग करके दिए गए व्यंजक में A का D से संबंध ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>A + B − C × D [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maternal Grandfather","hi":"नाना"},"2":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"},"3":{"en":"Paternal Grandfather","hi":"दादा"},"4":{"en":"Paternal Uncle","hi":"चाचा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"133\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"161\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M171 82V104M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">A+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">B−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">C−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">D</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>A is the father of D's mother C, so A is D's maternal grandfather.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Maternal Grandfather.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"133\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"161\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M171 82V104M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">A+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">B−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">C−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">D</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>A, D की माता C का पिता है, अतः A, D का नाना है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): नाना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074484","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many such letters are there in the word ADEPT, which are in the same position as in the English alphabet? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द ADEPT में ऐसे कितने अक्षर हैं जो उसी स्थान पर हैं जिस स्थान पर वे अंग्रेज़ी वर्णमाला में हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A (1st) = A is 1st in alphabet ✔<br>D (2nd) ✗, E (3rd) ✗, P (4th) ✗, T (5th) ✗<br>Count = 1<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"A (पहला) = वर्णमाला में भी पहला ✔<br>D (दूसरा) ✗, E (तीसरा) ✗, P (चौथा) ✗, T (पाँचवाँ) ✗<br>गिनती = 1<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074485","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Ravi and Seema are brother and sister. Amit and Vijay are the sons of Mohan and Radha. Radha is the mother-in-law of Seema's mother, Geeta. Tara, Tina, and Tripti are the daughters of Amit and the only cousins of Ravi. How many children does Vijay have? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रवि और सीमा भाई-बहन हैं। अमित और विजय, मोहन और राधा के पुत्र हैं। राधा, सीमा की माता गीता की सास है। तारा, टीना और तृप्ति, अमित की पुत्रियाँ हैं और रवि की एकमात्र चचेरी बहनें हैं। विजय की कितनी संतानें हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"0"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"363\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 363 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"221\" y=\"62\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M166 14H188M166 18H188M274 68H296M274 72H296M177 18V50M105 50H246M105 50V62M246 50V62M105 82V104M36 104H175M36 104V116M103 104V116M175 104V116M285 72V104M250 104H322M250 104V116M322 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"136\" y=\"22\">Mohan+</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"22\">Radha−</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"76\">Amit+</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"76\">Vijay+</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"76\">Geeta−</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"130\">Tara−</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"130\">Tina−</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"130\">Tripti−</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"130\">Ravi+</text><text x=\"322\" y=\"130\">Seema−</text></g><text x=\"182\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>Amit's daughters are Ravi's only cousins, so Ravi and Seema are Vijay's children; Vijay has 2 children.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"363\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 363 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"221\" y=\"62\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M166 14H188M166 18H188M274 68H296M274 72H296M177 18V50M105 50H246M105 50V62M246 50V62M105 82V104M36 104H175M36 104V116M103 104V116M175 104V116M285 72V104M250 104H322M250 104V116M322 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"136\" y=\"22\">Mohan+</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"22\">Radha−</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"76\">Amit+</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"76\">Vijay+</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"76\">Geeta−</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"130\">Tara−</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"130\">Tina−</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"130\">Tripti−</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"130\">Ravi+</text><text x=\"322\" y=\"130\">Seema−</text></g><text x=\"182\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>अमित की पुत्रियाँ ही रवि की एकमात्र चचेरी बहनें हैं, अतः रवि और सीमा विजय की संतान हैं; विजय की 2 संतानें हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074486","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">96</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">56</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न की पहचान करके लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">96</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">56</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"52"},"2":{"en":"66"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"74"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Column-wise: third = (second)² − (first)²<br>10² − 2² = 96 ✔, 9² − 5² = 56 ✔<br>8² − 4² = 64 − 16 = 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 48.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार: तीसरी = (दूसरी)² − (पहली)²<br>10² − 2² = 96 ✔, 9² − 5² = 56 ✔<br>8² − 4² = 64 − 16 = 48<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074487","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A centre code follows the sequence of [n<sup>2</sup>] − [n<sup>3</sup>]. Which of the following centre code does not follow this pattern? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक केंद्र कोड [n<sup>2</sup>] − [n<sup>3</sup>] अनुक्रम का पालन करता है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा केंद्र कोड इस पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16-64"},"2":{"en":"25-125"},"3":{"en":"36-216"},"4":{"en":"49-345"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"16-64 = 4² - 4³ ✔, 25-125 = 5² - 5³ ✔, 36-216 = 6² - 6³ ✔<br>49 = 7² but 7³ = 343, not 345 → 49-345 does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 49-345.</b>","hi":"16-64 = 4² - 4³ ✔, 25-125 = 5² - 5³ ✔, 36-216 = 6² - 6³ ✔<br>49 = 7² पर 7³ = 343 है, 345 नहीं → 49-345 पालन नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 49-345 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074488","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न की पहचान करके लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Column-wise: third = first + 2 × second<br>6 + 2 × 4 = 14 ✔, 9 + 2 × 7 = 23 ✔<br>13 + 2 × ? = 33 → ? = 10<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार: तीसरी = पहली + 2 × दूसरी<br>6 + 2 × 4 = 14 ✔, 9 + 2 × 7 = 23 ✔<br>13 + 2 × ? = 33 → ? = 10<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074489","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>WHE, SIA, OJW, ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला के पैटर्न का अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>WHE, SIA, OJW, ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"KKS"},"2":{"en":"KOS"},"3":{"en":"KKT"},"4":{"en":"KKR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1st letters: W, S, O, K (−4)<br>2nd letters: H, I, J, K (+1)<br>3rd letters: E, A, W, S (−4)<br>Next = KKS<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): KKS.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर: W, S, O, K (−4)<br>दूसरे अक्षर: H, I, J, K (+1)<br>तीसरे अक्षर: E, A, W, S (−4)<br>अगला = KKS<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): KKS है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074490","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32, 1056"},"2":{"en":"28, 816"},"3":{"en":"23, 552"},"4":{"en":"19, 380"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Rule: n × (n + 1)<br>32 × 33 = 1056 ✔, 23 × 24 = 552 ✔, 19 × 20 = 380 ✔<br>28 × 29 = 812, not 816 → odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 28, 816.</b>","hi":"नियम: n × (n + 1)<br>32 × 33 = 1056 ✔, 23 × 24 = 552 ✔, 19 × 20 = 380 ✔<br>28 × 29 = 812, 816 नहीं → विषम युग्म<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 28, 816 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074491","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"<b>Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.</b><br>You are a hospital administrator. Patients are complaining about long waiting times, and staff members are blaming each other for the delays. What would you do? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>प्रश्न को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और सबसे उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।</b><br>आप एक अस्पताल प्रशासक हैं। मरीज़ लंबे प्रतीक्षा समय की शिकायत कर रहे हैं, और कर्मचारी देरी के लिए एक-दूसरे को दोष दे रहे हैं। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Warn all staff members without examining the actual causes of delays.","hi":"देरी के वास्तविक कारणों की जाँच किए बिना सभी कर्मचारियों को चेतावनी देंगे।"},"2":{"en":"Take no action because disagreements among staff are very common.","hi":"कोई कार्रवाई नहीं करेंगे क्योंकि कर्मचारियों में असहमति बहुत आम है।"},"3":{"en":"Replace the entire team and recruit new employees immediately instead.","hi":"पूरी टीम को बदलकर तुरंत नए कर्मचारी भर्ती करेंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Review the process carefully and involve staff in improving services.","hi":"प्रक्रिया की ध्यानपूर्वक समीक्षा करेंगे और सेवाओं में सुधार में कर्मचारियों को शामिल करेंगे।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The root cause of the delay must be found and fixed with the team's help.<br>Warning without enquiry, doing nothing or replacing everyone does not solve the problem.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Review the process carefully and involve staff in improving services.</b>","hi":"देरी का मूल कारण खोजकर टीम की सहायता से उसे दूर करना चाहिए।<br>बिना जाँच चेतावनी देना, कुछ न करना या सबको बदल देना समस्या का समाधान नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): प्रक्रिया की ध्यानपूर्वक समीक्षा करेंगे और सेवाओं में सुधार में कर्मचारियों को शामिल करेंगे। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074492","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the best alternative.<br>@# &#36; : &#36; #@ :: &amp;*! : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सबसे उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br>@# &#36; : &#36; #@ :: &amp;*! : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"!&amp;*"},"2":{"en":"*&amp;!"},"3":{"en":"&amp;!*"},"4":{"en":"!*&amp;"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"@#&#36; → &#36;#@: the symbols are written in reverse order<br>&amp;*! → !*&amp;<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): !*&amp;.</b>","hi":"@#&#36; → &#36;#@: प्रतीकों को उल्टे क्रम में लिखा गया है<br>&amp;*! → !*&amp;<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): !*&amp; है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074493","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>ZYX : WVU :: TSR : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्न चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आना चाहिए?<br>ZYX : WVU :: TSR : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPO"},"2":{"en":"RQP"},"3":{"en":"PON"},"4":{"en":"QPN"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter moves 3 steps back: Z → W, Y → V, X → U<br>T → Q, S → P, R → O → QPO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QPO.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर 3 स्थान पीछे जाता है: Z → W, Y → V, X → U<br>T → Q, S → P, R → O → QPO<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): QPO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074494","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br>Statements<br>1. All contracts are agreements.<br>2. No agreement is unenforceable.<br>3. Some documents are contracts.<br>Conclusions<br>I. Some documents are agreements.<br>II. Some documents are not unenforceable.<br>III. No contract is unenforceable.<br>IV. Some agreements are documents. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में, कुछ कथन और उन पर आधारित निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानते हुए बताइए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करते हैं।<br>कथन<br>1. सभी अनुबंध समझौते हैं।<br>2. कोई भी समझौता अप्रवर्तनीय नहीं है।<br>3. कुछ दस्तावेज़ अनुबंध हैं।<br>निष्कर्ष<br>I. कुछ दस्तावेज़ समझौते हैं।<br>II. कुछ दस्तावेज़ अप्रवर्तनीय नहीं हैं।<br>III. कोई भी अनुबंध अप्रवर्तनीय नहीं है।<br>IV. कुछ समझौते दस्तावेज़ हैं। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I, II and III follow","hi":"केवल I, II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I, III and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, III और IV अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"All four follow","hi":"चारों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only I and III follow","hi":"केवल I और III अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Some documents are contracts → those are agreements: I ✔ and its converse IV ✔<br>Contracts are agreements and no agreement is unenforceable: III ✔<br>The documents that are contracts are not unenforceable: II ✔<br>All four follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): All four follow.</b>","hi":"कुछ दस्तावेज़ अनुबंध हैं → वे समझौते हैं: I ✔ और उसका विलोम IV ✔<br>अनुबंध समझौते हैं और कोई समझौता अप्रवर्तनीय नहीं: III ✔<br>जो दस्तावेज़ अनुबंध हैं वे अप्रवर्तनीय नहीं हैं: II ✔<br>चारों अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): चारों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074495","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"<b>Which sequence of operational signs will correctly replace the blanks to satisfy the following expression?</b><br>19 □ 5 □ 4 □ 2 = 37 [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>संक्रिया चिह्नों का कौन-सा क्रम रिक्त स्थानों में रखने पर निम्नलिखित व्यंजक संतुष्ट होगा?</b><br>19 □ 5 □ 4 □ 2 = 37 [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"×, −, ÷"},"2":{"en":"+, ×, −"},"3":{"en":"×, +, ÷"},"4":{"en":"+, ×, +"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Try +, ×, −: 19 + 5 × 4 − 2<br>= 19 + 20 − 2 = 37 ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): +, ×, −.</b>","hi":"+, ×, − रखने पर: 19 + 5 × 4 − 2<br>= 19 + 20 − 2 = 37 ✔<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): +, ×, − है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074496","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A company aims to improve customer satisfaction by upgrading its service quality.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All existing customers are currently dissatisfied.<br>II. The company believes service quality affects customer satisfaction. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हो, कथन का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करता/करते है/हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक कंपनी अपनी सेवा गुणवत्ता में सुधार करके ग्राहक संतुष्टि बढ़ाना चाहती है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी मौजूदा ग्राहक वर्तमान में असंतुष्ट हैं।<br>II. कंपनी मानती है कि सेवा गुणवत्ता ग्राहक संतुष्टि को प्रभावित करती है। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Improving satisfaction does not mean all customers are dissatisfied: I ✗<br>Upgrading service to raise satisfaction shows the company links the two: II ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"संतुष्टि बढ़ाने का अर्थ यह नहीं कि सभी ग्राहक असंतुष्ट हैं: I ✗<br>संतुष्टि के लिए सेवा सुधारना दर्शाता है कि कंपनी दोनों को जुड़ा मानती है: II ✔<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074497","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If ‘♦’ means +, ‘△’ means −, ‘★’ means ×, and ‘○’ means ÷, find (9 ♦ 6) ★ [(56 ○ 7) △ (2 ★ 2)]. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि ‘♦’ का अर्थ +, ‘△’ का अर्थ −, ‘★’ का अर्थ × और ‘○’ का अर्थ ÷ है, तो (9 ♦ 6) ★ [(56 ○ 7) △ (2 ★ 2)] ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"60"},"4":{"en":"80"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"(9 + 6) × [(56 ÷ 7) − (2 × 2)]<br>= 15 × (8 − 4) = 15 × 4 = 60<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60.</b>","hi":"(9 + 6) × [(56 ÷ 7) − (2 × 2)]<br>= 15 × (8 − 4) = 15 × 4 = 60<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074498","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A publishing house is launching a new magazine and is spending heavily on advertisements. To meet promotional expenses, it plans to cut unnecessary costs and raise funds from investors.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The new magazine has the potential to attract readers.<br>II. All investors will be willing to invest in the magazine. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ पूर्वधारणाएँ दी गई हैं। पूर्वधारणाओं को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक प्रकाशन गृह एक नई पत्रिका शुरू कर रहा है और विज्ञापनों पर भारी खर्च कर रहा है। प्रचार खर्च पूरा करने के लिए वह अनावश्यक लागत घटाने और निवेशकों से धन जुटाने की योजना बना रहा है।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. नई पत्रिका में पाठकों को आकर्षित करने की क्षमता है।<br>II. सभी निवेशक पत्रिका में निवेश करने के इच्छुक होंगे। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I अंतर्निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II अंतर्निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II अंतर्निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों अंतर्निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Heavy advertising makes sense only if the magazine can attract readers: I ✔<br>Raising funds does not assume that all investors will invest: II ✗ (\"all\" is too strong)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I is implicit.</b>","hi":"भारी विज्ञापन तभी सार्थक है जब पत्रिका पाठकों को आकर्षित कर सके: I ✔<br>धन जुटाने का अर्थ यह नहीं कि सभी निवेशक निवेश करेंगे: II ✗ (\"सभी\" बहुत प्रबल है)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I अंतर्निहित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074499","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"An office has a policy: “Employees who work overtime for more than 4 hours are entitled to a paid dinner voucher.” An employee works 3 hours and 55 minutes of overtime. He is starving and requests a voucher. As a manager, you know the policy is strict. What is your judgment? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कार्यालय की नीति है: “जो कर्मचारी 4 घंटे से अधिक ओवरटाइम करते हैं, वे सवेतन डिनर वाउचर के हकदार हैं।” एक कर्मचारी 3 घंटे 55 मिनट ओवरटाइम करता है। वह भूखा है और वाउचर माँगता है। एक प्रबंधक के रूप में, आप जानते हैं कि नीति सख्त है। आपका निर्णय क्या है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Deny the voucher to maintain strict discipline.","hi":"सख्त अनुशासन बनाए रखने के लिए वाउचर देने से मना करेंगे।"},"2":{"en":"Give the voucher as an exception to build rapport.","hi":"संबंध बनाने के लिए अपवाद के रूप में वाउचर देंगे।"},"3":{"en":"Reject voucher but allow 5-minute time log extension to meet threshold.","hi":"वाउचर अस्वीकार करेंगे लेकिन सीमा पूरी करने के लिए 5 मिनट का समय बढ़ाने देंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Approve the voucher and tell him to ignore the 4-hour policy in the future.","hi":"वाउचर स्वीकृत करेंगे और भविष्य में 4 घंटे की नीति को अनदेखा करने को कहेंगे।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The policy must be followed, but the employee can be allowed to complete the remaining 5 minutes and genuinely qualify.<br>This respects both the rule and the employee.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Reject voucher but allow 5-minute time log extension to meet threshold.</b>","hi":"नीति का पालन होना चाहिए, पर कर्मचारी को शेष 5 मिनट पूरे करके वास्तव में पात्र बनने दिया जा सकता है।<br>इससे नियम और कर्मचारी दोनों का सम्मान होता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): वाउचर अस्वीकार करेंगे लेकिन सीमा पूरी करने के लिए 5 मिनट का समय बढ़ाने देंगे। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074500","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>All apples are fruits.<br>All fruits are food.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All apples are food.<br>II. Some food are fruits. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। आपको दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्य रूप से ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए दोनों कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सभी सेब फल हैं।<br>सभी फल भोजन हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी सेब भोजन हैं।<br>II. कुछ भोजन फल हैं। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"All apples ⊂ fruits ⊂ food → All apples are food: I ✔<br>All fruits are food → Some food are fruits: II ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Both conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"सभी सेब ⊂ फल ⊂ भोजन → सभी सेब भोजन हैं: I ✔<br>सभी फल भोजन हैं → कुछ भोजन फल हैं: II ✔<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074501","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"AMOUNT\" is written as \"AnOvNu.\" How will \"DEPEND\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में, \"AMOUNT\" को \"AnOvNu.\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"DEPEND\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"DfPfNe"},"2":{"en":"DFpfNe"},"3":{"en":"DfpfnE"},"4":{"en":"DfPfnE"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Letters at odd places stay the same (capital); letters at even places move +1 and become small.<br>AMOUNT: A, M→n, O, U→v, N, T→u<br>DEPEND: D, E→f, P, E→f, N, D→e → DfPfNe<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): DfPfNe.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थानों के अक्षर वही (बड़े) रहते हैं; सम स्थानों के अक्षर +1 होकर छोटे हो जाते हैं।<br>AMOUNT: A, M→n, O, U→v, N, T→u<br>DEPEND: D, E→f, P, E→f, N, D→e → DfPfNe<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): DfPfNe है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074502","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given followed by three conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some flowers are trees.<br>All trees are rivers.<br>No river is a mountain.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some flowers are rivers.<br>II. All trees are mountains.<br>III. Some rivers are not mountains. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, तीन कथन और उनके बाद तीन निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्य रूप से ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ फूल पेड़ हैं।<br>सभी पेड़ नदियाँ हैं।<br>कोई नदी पहाड़ नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ फूल नदियाँ हैं।<br>II. सभी पेड़ पहाड़ हैं।<br>III. कुछ नदियाँ पहाड़ नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"All conclusions follow","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions II and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष II और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Some flowers are trees, all trees are rivers → Some flowers are rivers: I ✔<br>Trees are rivers and no river is a mountain → no tree is a mountain: II ✗<br>No river is a mountain → Some rivers are not mountains: III ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both conclusions I and III follow.</b>","hi":"कुछ फूल पेड़ हैं, सभी पेड़ नदियाँ हैं → कुछ फूल नदियाँ हैं: I ✔<br>पेड़ नदियाँ हैं और कोई नदी पहाड़ नहीं → कोई पेड़ पहाड़ नहीं: II ✗<br>कोई नदी पहाड़ नहीं → कुछ नदियाँ पहाड़ नहीं हैं: III ✔<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074503","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"An airline waives the rebooking fee if a request is made 24 hours or more before departure, provided the ticket is a Flex or Business class fare. For any requests made less than 24 hours before departure, a rebooking fee applies to all fare types — except that Elite-status passengers are always exempt from this fee.<br>Passenger details: Holds an Economy Saver fare, requests a change 3 hours before departure, and holds Elite status. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक एयरलाइन रीबुकिंग शुल्क माफ़ करती है यदि अनुरोध प्रस्थान से 24 घंटे या उससे पहले किया जाए, बशर्ते टिकट फ्लेक्स या बिज़नेस क्लास किराए का हो। प्रस्थान से 24 घंटे से कम समय पहले किए गए किसी भी अनुरोध पर सभी किराया प्रकारों पर रीबुकिंग शुल्क लगता है — सिवाय इसके कि एलीट-स्टेटस यात्रियों को इस शुल्क से हमेशा छूट रहती है।<br>यात्री विवरण: इकॉनमी सेवर किराया है, प्रस्थान से 3 घंटे पहले बदलाव का अनुरोध करता है, और एलीट स्टेटस रखता है। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Free rebooking","hi":"निःशुल्क रीबुकिंग"},"2":{"en":"Rebooking fee applies","hi":"रीबुकिंग शुल्क लगेगा"},"3":{"en":"Rebooking denied outright","hi":"रीबुकिंग सीधे अस्वीकार"},"4":{"en":"Refer to the duty supervisor","hi":"ड्यूटी पर्यवेक्षक के पास भेजें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The request is less than 24 hours before departure, so the fee would normally apply.<br>But Elite-status passengers are always exempt → Free rebooking.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Free rebooking.</b>","hi":"अनुरोध प्रस्थान से 24 घंटे से कम पहले है, अतः सामान्यतः शुल्क लगेगा।<br>लेकिन एलीट-स्टेटस यात्रियों को हमेशा छूट है → निःशुल्क रीबुकिंग।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): निःशुल्क रीबुकिंग है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074504","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Bauxite : Aluminium :: Cinnabar : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को सार्थक अंग्रेज़ी शब्द माना जाना चाहिए और उन्हें शब्द में अक्षरों/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर एक-दूसरे से संबंधित नहीं किया जाना चाहिए।)<br>Bauxite : Aluminium :: Cinnabar : ? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lead","hi":"सीसा (Lead)"},"2":{"en":"Mercury","hi":"पारा (Mercury)"},"3":{"en":"Zinc","hi":"जस्ता (Zinc)"},"4":{"en":"Tin","hi":"टिन (Tin)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Bauxite is the ore of Aluminium.<br>Cinnabar is the ore of Mercury.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Mercury.</b>","hi":"बॉक्साइट, एल्युमिनियम का अयस्क है।<br>सिनेबार, पारे (Mercury) का अयस्क है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): पारा (Mercury) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074505","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In each of the following questions, four options have been given, of which three are alike in some way and one is different. Choose the odd one out. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रत्येक प्रश्न में चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार से एक समान हैं और एक भिन्न है। विषम को चुनिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Japan – Yen","hi":"जापान – येन"},"2":{"en":"South Korea – Won","hi":"दक्षिण कोरिया – वॉन"},"3":{"en":"China – Yuan","hi":"चीन – युआन"},"4":{"en":"Vietnam – Baht","hi":"वियतनाम – बाट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Yen, Won and Yuan are the correct currencies of Japan, South Korea and China.<br>Vietnam's currency is the Dong; Baht belongs to Thailand.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Vietnam – Baht.</b>","hi":"येन, वॉन और युआन क्रमशः जापान, दक्षिण कोरिया और चीन की सही मुद्राएँ हैं।<br>वियतनाम की मुद्रा डोंग है; बाट थाईलैंड की मुद्रा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): वियतनाम – बाट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074506","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"The \"Goods and Services Tax (GST)\" council is responsible for making recommendations on various aspects of GST. Who chairs this council? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (GST)\" परिषद GST के विभिन्न पहलुओं पर सिफारिशें करने के लिए उत्तरदायी है। इस परिषद की अध्यक्षता कौन करता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The President of India","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति"},"2":{"en":"The Prime Minister of India","hi":"भारत के प्रधानमंत्री"},"3":{"en":"The Union Finance Minister","hi":"केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री"},"4":{"en":"The Governor of the Reserve Bank of India","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के गवर्नर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Union Finance Minister</b><br>Under <b>Article 279A</b>, the <b>GST Council</b> is chaired by the <b><u>Union Finance Minister</u></b>; the Union MoS (Finance) and State Finance Ministers are members.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Decisions need a <b>three-fourths majority</b>; Centre has one-third and States two-thirds of the vote weight.<br>• GST came into force on <b>1 July 2017</b>.<br>• The <b>101<sup>st</sup> Amendment (2016)</b> introduced GST.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 279A</b> के तहत <b>GST परिषद</b> की अध्यक्षता <b><u>केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री</u></b> करते हैं; केंद्रीय वित्त राज्य मंत्री और राज्यों के वित्त मंत्री इसके सदस्य हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• निर्णयों के लिए <b>तीन-चौथाई बहुमत</b> आवश्यक; केंद्र का मत भार एक-तिहाई और राज्यों का दो-तिहाई।<br>• GST <b>1 जुलाई 2017</b> से लागू हुआ।<br>• <b>101वें संशोधन (2016)</b> ने GST लागू किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074507","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"The \"Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management (FRBM) Act\" was enacted in India with the aim of bringing about fiscal discipline. Which of the following is a key target or provision of the FRBM Act? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में राजकोषीय अनुशासन लाने के उद्देश्य से \"राजकोषीय उत्तरदायित्व और बजट प्रबंधन (FRBM) अधिनियम\" बनाया गया। निम्नलिखित में से FRBM अधिनियम का प्रमुख लक्ष्य या प्रावधान कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To ensure a fixed exchange rate for the Indian Rupee.","hi":"भारतीय रुपये की निश्चित विनिमय दर सुनिश्चित करना।"},"2":{"en":"To set limits on the government's borrowing and mandate the reduction of fiscal deficit and revenue deficit.","hi":"सरकार के उधार पर सीमा तय करना और राजकोषीय घाटा व राजस्व घाटा कम करना अनिवार्य करना।"},"3":{"en":"To establish a national planning commission for economic development.","hi":"आर्थिक विकास के लिए राष्ट्रीय योजना आयोग स्थापित करना।"},"4":{"en":"To regulate the flow of foreign portfolio investment into the country.","hi":"देश में विदेशी पोर्टफोलियो निवेश के प्रवाह को विनियमित करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To set limits on the government's borrowing and mandate the reduction of fiscal deficit and revenue deficit.</b><br>The <b>FRBM Act, 2003</b> aims at fiscal discipline by <b><u>limiting government borrowing and requiring reduction of fiscal and revenue deficits</u></b> in a time-bound manner.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act came into force on <b>5 July 2004</b>; original fiscal deficit target was <b>3% of GDP</b>.<br>• The <b>N.K. Singh Committee (2016)</b> reviewed FRBM and suggested a debt-to-GDP target.<br>• The Act requires a <b>Medium-Term Fiscal Policy Statement</b> with the Budget.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सरकार के उधार पर सीमा तय करना और राजकोषीय घाटा व राजस्व घाटा कम करना अनिवार्य करना।</b><br><b>FRBM अधिनियम, 2003</b> का उद्देश्य <b><u>सरकारी उधार को सीमित करके और राजकोषीय व राजस्व घाटे को समयबद्ध तरीके से कम करना अनिवार्य करके</u></b> राजकोषीय अनुशासन लाना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अधिनियम <b>5 जुलाई 2004</b> से लागू हुआ; मूल राजकोषीय घाटा लक्ष्य <b>GDP का 3%</b> था।<br>• <b>एन.के. सिंह समिति (2016)</b> ने FRBM की समीक्षा की और ऋण-GDP लक्ष्य सुझाया।<br>• अधिनियम बजट के साथ <b>मध्यम अवधि राजकोषीय नीति विवरण</b> अनिवार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074508","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which sport is associated with the Thomas Cup? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"थॉमस कप किस खेल से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Badminton","hi":"बैडमिंटन"},"2":{"en":"Tennis","hi":"टेनिस"},"3":{"en":"Hockey","hi":"हॉकी"},"4":{"en":"Cricket","hi":"क्रिकेट"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Badminton</b><br>The <b>Thomas Cup</b> is the world men's team championship of <b><u>badminton</u></b>; India won it for the first time in <b>2022 (Bangkok)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Uber Cup</b> – women's team badminton; <b>Sudirman Cup</b> – mixed team.<br>• Other badminton trophies: <b>All England Championship</b>.<br>• Tennis: <b>Davis Cup</b> (men), Billie Jean King Cup (women).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बैडमिंटन</b><br><b>थॉमस कप</b> <b><u>बैडमिंटन</u></b> की विश्व पुरुष टीम चैंपियनशिप है; भारत ने इसे पहली बार <b>2022 (बैंकॉक)</b> में जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>उबेर कप</b> – महिला टीम बैडमिंटन; <b>सुदीरमन कप</b> – मिश्रित टीम।<br>• अन्य बैडमिंटन ट्रॉफ़ी: <b>ऑल इंग्लैंड चैंपियनशिप</b>।<br>• टेनिस: <b>डेविस कप</b> (पुरुष), बिली जीन किंग कप (महिला)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074509","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which event did India earn its first World Championship gold in athletics? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत ने एथलेटिक्स में अपना पहला विश्व चैंपियनशिप स्वर्ण किस स्पर्धा में जीता? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Men’s Javelin Throw","hi":"पुरुष भाला फेंक"},"2":{"en":"Women’s Long Jump","hi":"महिला लंबी कूद"},"3":{"en":"Women’s 400m","hi":"महिला 400 मीटर"},"4":{"en":"Men’s Steeplechase","hi":"पुरुष स्टीपलचेज़"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Men’s Javelin Throw</b><br><b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won India's first World Athletics Championships gold in the <b><u>men's javelin throw</u></b> at <b>Budapest 2023</b> (88.17 m).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Neeraj won Olympic gold at <b>Tokyo 2020</b> and silver at <b>Paris 2024</b>.<br>• India's first World Championships medal: <b>Anju Bobby George</b> (long jump bronze, 2003).<br>• He crossed <b>90 m</b> for the first time in May 2025 (Doha Diamond League).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पुरुष भाला फेंक</b><br><b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने <b>बुडापेस्ट 2023</b> में <b><u>पुरुष भाला फेंक</u></b> (88.17 m) में भारत का पहला विश्व एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप स्वर्ण जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नीरज ने <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> में ओलंपिक स्वर्ण और <b>पेरिस 2024</b> में रजत जीता।<br>• भारत का पहला विश्व चैंपियनशिप पदक: <b>अंजू बॉबी जॉर्ज</b> (लंबी कूद कांस्य, 2003)।<br>• उन्होंने मई 2025 (दोहा डायमंड लीग) में पहली बार <b>90 m</b> पार किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074510","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Where was the setting for the final match of the 2021 Indian Super League season? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2021 इंडियन सुपर लीग सीज़न का फाइनल मैच कहाँ खेला गया? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Margao","hi":"मडगाँव"},"2":{"en":"Kochi","hi":"कोच्चि"},"3":{"en":"Kolkata","hi":"कोलकाता"},"4":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Margao</b><br>The <b>2020–21 ISL</b> season was played entirely in Goa (bio-bubble) and the final was held at the <b>Fatorda Stadium, <u>Margao</u></b>, where <b>Mumbai City FC</b> beat ATK Mohun Bagan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2021–22 final was also held at Fatorda, won by <b>Hyderabad FC</b>.<br>• ISL began in <b>2014</b>.<br>• <b>Durand Cup</b> is Asia's oldest football tournament (1888).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मडगाँव</b><br><b>2020–21 ISL</b> सीज़न पूरी तरह गोवा (बायो-बबल) में खेला गया और फाइनल <b>फ़ातोर्डा स्टेडियम, <u>मडगाँव</u></b> में हुआ, जहाँ <b>मुंबई सिटी FC</b> ने ATK मोहन बागान को हराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2021–22 का फाइनल भी फ़ातोर्डा में हुआ, जिसे <b>हैदराबाद FC</b> ने जीता।<br>• ISL <b>2014</b> में शुरू हुई।<br>• <b>डूरंड कप</b> एशिया का सबसे पुराना फ़ुटबॉल टूर्नामेंट (1888) है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074511","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"According to BSA, if a person refuses to answer a material question in court what&nbsp; are the consequences? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"BSA के अनुसार यदि कोई व्यक्ति न्यायालय में किसी तात्विक प्रश्न का उत्तर देने से इनकार करता है तो क्या परिणाम होते हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Adverse inference may be drawn","hi":"प्रतिकूल निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है"},"2":{"en":"They are held guilty automatically","hi":"उन्हें स्वतः दोषी ठहराया जाता है"},"3":{"en":"Their evidence is expunged","hi":"उनका साक्ष्य हटा दिया जाता है"},"4":{"en":"The case is dismissed","hi":"मामला खारिज कर दिया जाता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Adverse inference may be drawn</b><br>Under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, when a witness refuses to answer a relevant question, the Court <b><u>may draw an adverse inference</u></b> (presumption) against him; he is not automatically held guilty.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>\"May presume\"</b> provisions give the Court discretion.<br>• The BSA replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> from <b>1 July 2024</b>.<br>• Article 20(3) protects an accused against <b>self-incrimination</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – प्रतिकूल निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है</b><br>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम के तहत जब कोई गवाह किसी सुसंगत प्रश्न का उत्तर देने से इनकार करता है, तो न्यायालय उसके विरुद्ध <b><u>प्रतिकूल निष्कर्ष (उपधारणा) निकाल सकता है</u></b>; उसे स्वतः दोषी नहीं ठहराया जाता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>\"उपधारणा कर सकेगा\"</b> वाले प्रावधान न्यायालय को विवेकाधिकार देते हैं।<br>• BSA ने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया।<br>• अनुच्छेद 20(3) अभियुक्त को <b>आत्म-अभिशंसन</b> से संरक्षण देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074512","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"Who was the first woman chairperson of India's markets regulator, Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI)? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के बाज़ार नियामक, भारतीय प्रतिभूति और विनिमय बोर्ड (SEBI) की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष कौन थीं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arundhati Bhattacharya","hi":"अरुंधति भट्टाचार्य"},"2":{"en":"Madhabi Puri Buch","hi":"माधबी पुरी बुच"},"3":{"en":"Naina Lal Kidwai","hi":"नैना लाल किदवई"},"4":{"en":"Chitra Ramkrishna","hi":"चित्रा रामकृष्ण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Madhabi Puri Buch</b><br><b><u>Madhabi Puri Buch</u></b> became the first woman Chairperson of <b>SEBI</b> in <b>March 2022</b>. She was succeeded by <b>Tuhin Kanta Pandey</b> in March 2025.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SEBI was set up in <b>1988</b> and got statutory powers in <b>1992</b>; HQ <b>Mumbai</b>.<br>• <b>Arundhati Bhattacharya</b> – first woman Chairperson of <b>SBI</b>.<br>• <b>Chitra Ramkrishna</b> – former MD of <b>NSE</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – माधबी पुरी बुच</b><br><b><u>माधबी पुरी बुच</u></b> <b>मार्च 2022</b> में <b>SEBI</b> की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष बनीं। मार्च 2025 में <b>तुहिन कांत पांडे</b> उनके उत्तराधिकारी बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• SEBI <b>1988</b> में बना और <b>1992</b> में वैधानिक शक्तियाँ मिलीं; मुख्यालय <b>मुंबई</b>।<br>• <b>अरुंधति भट्टाचार्य</b> – <b>SBI</b> की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष।<br>• <b>चित्रा रामकृष्ण</b> – <b>NSE</b> की पूर्व MD।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074513","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who is the 26<sup>th</sup> Governor of the Reserve Bank of India since December 2024? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिसंबर 2024 से भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के 26वें गवर्नर कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Urjit Patel","hi":"उर्जित पटेल"},"2":{"en":"Sanjay Malhotra","hi":"संजय मल्होत्रा"},"3":{"en":"D. Subbarao","hi":"डी. सुब्बाराव"},"4":{"en":"Raghuram Rajan","hi":"रघुराम राजन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sanjay Malhotra</b><br><b><u>Sanjay Malhotra</u></b> took charge as the <b>26<sup>th</sup> Governor of RBI</b> on <b>11 December 2024</b>, succeeding Shaktikanta Das.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He was earlier the <b>Revenue Secretary</b>, Ministry of Finance.<br>• First RBI Governor: <b>Sir Osborne Smith</b>; first Indian Governor: <b>C.D. Deshmukh</b>.<br>• <b>Urjit Patel</b> was the 24<sup>th</sup> and <b>Shaktikanta Das</b> the 25<sup>th</sup> Governor.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संजय मल्होत्रा</b><br><b><u>संजय मल्होत्रा</u></b> ने <b>11 दिसंबर 2024</b> को शक्तिकांत दास के बाद <b>RBI के 26वें गवर्नर</b> का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे पहले वित्त मंत्रालय में <b>राजस्व सचिव</b> थे।<br>• RBI के पहले गवर्नर: <b>सर ऑस्बोर्न स्मिथ</b>; पहले भारतीय गवर्नर: <b>सी.डी. देशमुख</b>।<br>• <b>उर्जित पटेल</b> 24वें और <b>शक्तिकांत दास</b> 25वें गवर्नर थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074514","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Gupta Dynasty","question":{"en":"Who among the following rulers is known as the Napoleon of India? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित शासकों में से किसे भारत का नेपोलियन कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Samudragupta","hi":"समुद्रगुप्त"},"2":{"en":"Chandragupta II","hi":"चंद्रगुप्त द्वितीय"},"3":{"en":"Chandragupta Maurya","hi":"चंद्रगुप्त मौर्य"},"4":{"en":"Kanishka","hi":"कनिष्क"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Samudragupta</b><br>Historian <b>V.A. Smith</b> called <b><u>Samudragupta</u></b> the <b>\"Napoleon of India\"</b> because of his extensive military conquests described in the <b>Prayaga Prashasti</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Prayaga Prashasti was written by his court poet <b>Harisena</b>.<br>• Samudragupta performed the <b>Ashvamedha</b> sacrifice and was called <b>Kaviraja</b>.<br>• <b>Chandragupta II</b> is known as <b>Vikramaditya</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – समुद्रगुप्त</b><br>इतिहासकार <b>वी.ए. स्मिथ</b> ने <b>प्रयाग प्रशस्ति</b> में वर्णित व्यापक सैन्य विजयों के कारण <b><u>समुद्रगुप्त</u></b> को <b>\"भारत का नेपोलियन\"</b> कहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रयाग प्रशस्ति उनके दरबारी कवि <b>हरिषेण</b> ने लिखी।<br>• समुद्रगुप्त ने <b>अश्वमेध</b> यज्ञ किया और उन्हें <b>कविराज</b> कहा गया।<br>• <b>चंद्रगुप्त द्वितीय</b> को <b>विक्रमादित्य</b> कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074515","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"Which of the following Census years has India recorded the highest annual exponential population growth rate? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस जनगणना वर्ष में भारत ने सर्वाधिक वार्षिक घातांकी जनसंख्या वृद्धि दर दर्ज की? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1971"},"2":{"en":"1981"},"3":{"en":"1991"},"4":{"en":"2001"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1971</b><br>The highest <b>annual exponential growth rate</b> (about <b>2.20%</b>) was recorded in the decade <b>1961–71</b>, i.e., the Census of <b><u>1971</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The highest <b>decadal growth rate</b> (24.80%) was also in 1961–71.<br>• <b>1921</b> is called the \"Year of Great Divide\"; only decade of negative growth: <b>1911–21</b>.<br>• Census 2011 decadal growth: <b>17.7%</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1971</b><br>सर्वाधिक <b>वार्षिक घातांकी वृद्धि दर</b> (लगभग <b>2.20%</b>) <b>1961–71</b> के दशक, अर्थात् <b><u>1971</u></b> की जनगणना में दर्ज हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सर्वाधिक <b>दशकीय वृद्धि दर</b> (24.80%) भी 1961–71 में थी।<br>• <b>1921</b> को \"महाविभाजन वर्ष\" कहा जाता है; ऋणात्मक वृद्धि वाला एकमात्र दशक: <b>1911–21</b>।<br>• जनगणना 2011 की दशकीय वृद्धि: <b>17.7%</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074516","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"Which of the following correctly describes the structure introduced by Pitt’s India Act? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट द्वारा शुरू की गई संरचना का सही वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only the Governor-General had full authority.","hi":"केवल गवर्नर-जनरल के पास पूर्ण अधिकार था।"},"2":{"en":"Board of Control had three directors and reported to the Company.","hi":"नियंत्रण बोर्ड में तीन निदेशक थे और वह कंपनी को रिपोर्ट करता था।"},"3":{"en":"Board of Control included cabinet ministers and supervised Indian governance.","hi":"नियंत्रण बोर्ड में कैबिनेट मंत्री शामिल थे और वह भारतीय शासन की निगरानी करता था।"},"4":{"en":"A royal commission was sent to directly govern India.","hi":"भारत पर सीधे शासन के लिए एक शाही आयोग भेजा गया।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Board of Control included cabinet ministers and supervised Indian governance.</b><br><b>Pitt's India Act, 1784</b> set up a <b><u>Board of Control</u></b> of six members, including the Chancellor of the Exchequer and a Secretary of State (cabinet ministers), to <b>supervise the civil, military and revenue affairs</b> of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It created a <b>dual system of control</b> – Board of Control (Crown) and Court of Directors (Company).<br>• Company's territories in India were called <b>\"British possessions in India\"</b> for the first time.<br>• It was passed in the time of PM <b>William Pitt the Younger</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नियंत्रण बोर्ड में कैबिनेट मंत्री शामिल थे और वह भारतीय शासन की निगरानी करता था।</b><br><b>पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट, 1784</b> ने छह सदस्यों वाला <b><u>नियंत्रण बोर्ड</u></b> बनाया, जिसमें राजकोष के चांसलर और एक राज्य सचिव (कैबिनेट मंत्री) शामिल थे, ताकि भारत के <b>नागरिक, सैन्य और राजस्व मामलों की निगरानी</b> की जा सके।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने <b>द्वैध नियंत्रण प्रणाली</b> बनाई – नियंत्रण बोर्ड (क्राउन) और निदेशक मंडल (कंपनी)।<br>• पहली बार कंपनी के भारतीय क्षेत्रों को <b>\"भारत में ब्रिटिश अधिकृत क्षेत्र\"</b> कहा गया।<br>• यह प्रधानमंत्री <b>विलियम पिट द यंगर</b> के समय पारित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074517","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Jainism and Buddhism","question":{"en":"The Second Jain Council was held in 512 CE at Valabhi (Gujarat) under the chairmanship of which Jain acharya? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"द्वितीय जैन संगीति 512 ई. में वल्लभी (गुजरात) में किस जैन आचार्य की अध्यक्षता में आयोजित हुई? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Devardhigani Kshamashraman","hi":"देवर्धिगणि क्षमाश्रमण"},"2":{"en":"Acharya Bhadrabahu Swamy","hi":"आचार्य भद्रबाहु स्वामी"},"3":{"en":"Acharya Sthulabhadra Muni","hi":"आचार्य स्थूलभद्र मुनि"},"4":{"en":"Vardhamana Mahavira Swami","hi":"वर्धमान महावीर स्वामी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Devardhigani Kshamashraman</b><br>The <b>Second Jain Council</b> at <b>Valabhi</b> was presided over by <b><u>Devardhigani Kshamashraman</u></b>; the <b>12 Angas</b> and 12 Upangas were compiled in writing.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>First Jain Council</b> – Pataliputra (c. 300 BCE), presided by <b>Sthulabhadra</b>, under Chandragupta Maurya.<br>• <b>Bhadrabahu</b> led Jains to the south (Shravanabelagola) during a famine.<br>• Jainism split into <b>Digambara and Shvetambara</b> sects.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – देवर्धिगणि क्षमाश्रमण</b><br><b>वल्लभी</b> में <b>द्वितीय जैन संगीति</b> की अध्यक्षता <b><u>देवर्धिगणि क्षमाश्रमण</u></b> ने की; इसमें <b>12 अंग</b> और 12 उपांग लिखित रूप में संकलित हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>प्रथम जैन संगीति</b> – पाटलिपुत्र (लगभग 300 ई.पू.), अध्यक्ष <b>स्थूलभद्र</b>, चंद्रगुप्त मौर्य के समय।<br>• अकाल के समय <b>भद्रबाहु</b> जैनों को दक्षिण (श्रवणबेलगोला) ले गए।<br>• जैन धर्म <b>दिगंबर और श्वेतांबर</b> संप्रदायों में बँटा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074518","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"Which Article of the Indian Constitution specifies the languages to be used for transacting business in Parliament? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद संसद में कार्य संचालन हेतु प्रयुक्त भाषाओं को निर्दिष्ट करता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 110","hi":"अनुच्छेद 110"},"2":{"en":"Article 120","hi":"अनुच्छेद 120"},"3":{"en":"Article 121","hi":"अनुच्छेद 121"},"4":{"en":"Article 122","hi":"अनुच्छेद 122"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 120</b><br><b><u>Article 120</u></b> provides that business in Parliament shall be transacted in <b>Hindi or English</b>; a member who cannot express himself in either may address the House in his <b>mother tongue</b> with the Presiding Officer's permission.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Art. 110</b> – definition of Money Bill.<br>• <b>Art. 121</b> – no discussion in Parliament on conduct of SC/HC judges.<br>• <b>Art. 122</b> – courts not to inquire into proceedings of Parliament; <b>Art. 210</b> – language in State Legislatures.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुच्छेद 120</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 120</u></b> के अनुसार संसद में कार्य <b>हिंदी या अंग्रेज़ी</b> में होगा; जो सदस्य इनमें से किसी में अपनी बात नहीं कह सकता, वह पीठासीन अधिकारी की अनुमति से अपनी <b>मातृभाषा</b> में सदन को संबोधित कर सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनु. 110</b> – धन विधेयक की परिभाषा।<br>• <b>अनु. 121</b> – सर्वोच्च/उच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों के आचरण पर संसद में चर्चा नहीं।<br>• <b>अनु. 122</b> – न्यायालय संसद की कार्यवाही की जाँच नहीं करेंगे; <b>अनु. 210</b> – राज्य विधानमंडल की भाषा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074519","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Force and Laws of Motion","question":{"en":"What is the term for the natural tendency of an object to resist any change in its state of rest or uniform motion? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी वस्तु की अपनी विराम अवस्था या एकसमान गति की अवस्था में किसी भी परिवर्तन का विरोध करने की प्राकृतिक प्रवृत्ति को क्या कहते हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Force applied","hi":"लगाया गया बल"},"2":{"en":"Acceleration","hi":"त्वरण"},"3":{"en":"Inertia of the object","hi":"वस्तु का जड़त्व"},"4":{"en":"Momentum of an object","hi":"वस्तु का संवेग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Inertia of the object</b><br>The tendency of a body to resist a change in its state of rest or uniform motion is called <b><u>inertia</u></b>; it is the basis of <b>Newton's first law of motion</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Mass</b> is the measure of inertia – heavier bodies have more inertia.<br>• Types: <b>inertia of rest, inertia of motion, inertia of direction</b>.<br>• Galileo first gave the idea of inertia; Newton's first law is called the <b>law of inertia</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वस्तु का जड़त्व</b><br>किसी वस्तु की विराम या एकसमान गति की अवस्था में परिवर्तन का विरोध करने की प्रवृत्ति <b><u>जड़त्व (Inertia)</u></b> कहलाती है; यह <b>न्यूटन के गति के प्रथम नियम</b> का आधार है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>द्रव्यमान</b> जड़त्व का माप है – भारी वस्तुओं में अधिक जड़त्व होता है।<br>• प्रकार: <b>विराम का जड़त्व, गति का जड़त्व, दिशा का जड़त्व</b>।<br>• गैलीलियो ने सबसे पहले जड़त्व का विचार दिया; न्यूटन के प्रथम नियम को <b>जड़त्व का नियम</b> कहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074520","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Which African country lies on the western rim of the Indian Ocean? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा अफ्रीकी देश हिंद महासागर के पश्चिमी किनारे पर स्थित है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kenya","hi":"केन्या"},"2":{"en":"Libya","hi":"लीबिया"},"3":{"en":"Tunisia","hi":"ट्यूनीशिया"},"4":{"en":"Morocco","hi":"मोरक्को"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Kenya</b><br><b><u>Kenya</u></b> lies on the <b>east coast of Africa</b>, i.e., the western rim of the Indian Ocean. Libya and Tunisia face the Mediterranean, and Morocco the Atlantic.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kenya's main port: <b>Mombasa</b>; capital <b>Nairobi</b>.<br>• Other African Indian Ocean countries: <b>Somalia, Tanzania, Mozambique, South Africa</b>.<br>• The Equator passes through Kenya.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केन्या</b><br><b><u>केन्या</u></b> <b>अफ्रीका के पूर्वी तट</b> पर, अर्थात् हिंद महासागर के पश्चिमी किनारे पर स्थित है। लीबिया और ट्यूनीशिया भूमध्य सागर और मोरक्को अटलांटिक की ओर हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• केन्या का मुख्य बंदरगाह: <b>मोम्बासा</b>; राजधानी <b>नैरोबी</b>।<br>• हिंद महासागर तट के अन्य अफ्रीकी देश: <b>सोमालिया, तंज़ानिया, मोज़ाम्बिक, दक्षिण अफ्रीका</b>।<br>• भूमध्य रेखा केन्या से होकर गुज़रती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074521","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A Chief Judicial Magistrate issues an administrative order redistributing criminal cases among the Judicial Magistrates subordinate to him. One of the Magistrates challenges the order, arguing that only the Sessions Judge has the authority to distribute judicial business. Which of the following is correct under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट अपने अधीनस्थ न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों के बीच आपराधिक मामलों का पुनर्वितरण करने वाला प्रशासनिक आदेश जारी करता है। एक मजिस्ट्रेट यह तर्क देते हुए आदेश को चुनौती देता है कि केवल सत्र न्यायाधीश को न्यायिक कार्य वितरित करने का अधिकार है। भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से क्या सही है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only the sessions judge may distribute magistrate business.","hi":"केवल सत्र न्यायाधीश मजिस्ट्रेट का कार्य वितरित कर सकता है।"},"2":{"en":"Chief Judicial Magistrate empowered to distribute work among Judicial Magistrates.","hi":"मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों के बीच कार्य वितरित करने के लिए सशक्त है।"},"3":{"en":"Business distribution requires approval of the executive magistrate.","hi":"कार्य वितरण के लिए कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट की स्वीकृति आवश्यक है।"},"4":{"en":"The High Court alone may allocate all criminal cases.","hi":"केवल उच्च न्यायालय ही सभी आपराधिक मामलों का आवंटन कर सकता है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chief Judicial Magistrate empowered to distribute work among Judicial Magistrates.</b><br>Under <b>Section 15 of BNSS</b> (old CrPC Sec. 15), the <b><u>Chief Judicial Magistrate</u></b> may, subject to the control of the High Court, make rules or give special orders for the <b>distribution of business</b> among the Judicial Magistrates subordinate to him.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Every Judicial Magistrate is <b>subordinate to the CJM</b>, who is subordinate to the <b>Sessions Judge</b>.<br>• The Sessions Judge distributes business among Additional Sessions Judges.<br>• BNSS has <b>531 sections</b>; in force from <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों के बीच कार्य वितरित करने के लिए सशक्त है।</b><br><b>BNSS की धारा 15</b> (पुरानी CrPC धारा 15) के तहत <b><u>मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट</u></b> उच्च न्यायालय के नियंत्रण के अधीन अपने अधीनस्थ न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेटों के बीच <b>कार्य के वितरण</b> के लिए नियम बना सकता है या विशेष आदेश दे सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रत्येक न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट <b>CJM के अधीनस्थ</b> है, और CJM <b>सत्र न्यायाधीश</b> के अधीनस्थ है।<br>• सत्र न्यायाधीश अपर सत्र न्यायाधीशों के बीच कार्य वितरित करता है।<br>• BNSS में <b>531 धाराएँ</b> हैं; <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से लागू।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074522","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"In India, under which situation can Parliament legislate on a subject in the State List without declaring a national emergency? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में किस स्थिति में संसद राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल घोषित किए बिना राज्य सूची के किसी विषय पर कानून बना सकती है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"When the Lok Sabha passes a resolution by simple majority.","hi":"जब लोकसभा साधारण बहुमत से संकल्प पारित करे।"},"2":{"en":"Rajya Sabha passes a resolution with a two-thirds majority of members present and voting.","hi":"राज्यसभा उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों के दो-तिहाई बहुमत से संकल्प पारित करे।"},"3":{"en":"When the President issues an ordinance.","hi":"जब राष्ट्रपति अध्यादेश जारी करें।"},"4":{"en":"When the Supreme Court advises the union government.","hi":"जब सर्वोच्च न्यायालय केंद्र सरकार को सलाह दे।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Rajya Sabha passes a resolution with a two-thirds majority of members present and voting.</b><br>Under <b>Article 249</b>, if the <b><u>Rajya Sabha passes a resolution by a two-thirds majority of members present and voting</u></b> that it is necessary in the national interest, Parliament can make laws on a State List subject.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The resolution is valid for <b>one year</b> and can be extended.<br>• Other cases: <b>Art. 250</b> (National Emergency), <b>Art. 252</b> (two or more States request), <b>Art. 253</b> (international agreements).<br>• Also during <b>President's Rule</b> (Art. 356).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राज्यसभा उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों के दो-तिहाई बहुमत से संकल्प पारित करे।</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 249</b> के तहत यदि <b><u>राज्यसभा उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों के दो-तिहाई बहुमत से संकल्प पारित करे</u></b> कि राष्ट्रीय हित में यह आवश्यक है, तो संसद राज्य सूची के विषय पर कानून बना सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संकल्प <b>एक वर्ष</b> के लिए वैध है और बढ़ाया जा सकता है।<br>• अन्य स्थितियाँ: <b>अनु. 250</b> (राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल), <b>अनु. 252</b> (दो या अधिक राज्यों का अनुरोध), <b>अनु. 253</b> (अंतर्राष्ट्रीय समझौते)।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रपति शासन</b> (अनु. 356) के दौरान भी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074523","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"What was the primary objective of granting Maharatna, Navratna and Miniratna status to selected Central Public Sector Enterprises under the post-1991 economic reforms? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के बाद के आर्थिक सुधारों के तहत चयनित केंद्रीय सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उद्यमों को महारत्न, नवरत्न और मिनीरत्न का दर्जा देने का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To increase Government ownership in all sectors","hi":"सभी क्षेत्रों में सरकारी स्वामित्व बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"To expand industrial licensing and price regulation","hi":"औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग और मूल्य विनियमन का विस्तार"},"3":{"en":"To replace private investment with public investment","hi":"निजी निवेश को सार्वजनिक निवेश से बदलना"},"4":{"en":"To enhance autonomy and improve competitiveness","hi":"स्वायत्तता बढ़ाना और प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता में सुधार"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – To enhance autonomy and improve competitiveness</b><br>The Ratna status gave PSUs <b>greater managerial and operational autonomy</b> in decision-making, so as to <b><u>improve efficiency and competitiveness</u></b> (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Navratna</b> scheme – 1997; <b>Miniratna</b> – 1997; <b>Maharatna</b> – 2009.<br>• First Maharatnas: <b>NTPC, ONGC, SAIL, IOCL</b>.<br>• Maharatnas can invest up to <b>₹5,000 crore</b> without government approval.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – स्वायत्तता बढ़ाना और प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता में सुधार</b><br>रत्न दर्जे ने PSU को निर्णय लेने में <b>अधिक प्रबंधकीय और परिचालन स्वायत्तता</b> दी, ताकि <b><u>दक्षता और प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता में सुधार</u></b> हो (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नवरत्न</b> योजना – 1997; <b>मिनीरत्न</b> – 1997; <b>महारत्न</b> – 2009।<br>• पहले महारत्न: <b>NTPC, ONGC, SAIL, IOCL</b>।<br>• महारत्न सरकारी स्वीकृति के बिना <b>₹5,000 करोड़</b> तक निवेश कर सकते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074524","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Who was the Governor of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) during the 1991 balance of payments crisis? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के भुगतान संतुलन संकट के दौरान भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक (RBI) के गवर्नर कौन थे? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C. Rangarajan","hi":"सी. रंगराजन"},"2":{"en":"I.G. Patel","hi":"आई.जी. पटेल"},"3":{"en":"Manmohan Singh","hi":"मनमोहन सिंह"},"4":{"en":"S. Venkitaramanan","hi":"एस. वेंकटरमणन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – S. Venkitaramanan</b><br><b><u>S. Venkitaramanan</u></b> was RBI Governor from <b>1990 to 1992</b>, and handled the 1991 BoP crisis, including the pledging of gold.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>C. Rangarajan</b> succeeded him (1992–97).<br>• <b>Manmohan Singh</b> was RBI Governor in 1982–85 and Finance Minister in 1991.<br>• <b>I.G. Patel</b> was Governor in 1977–82.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – एस. वेंकटरमणन</b><br><b><u>एस. वेंकटरमणन</u></b> <b>1990 से 1992</b> तक RBI गवर्नर थे और उन्होंने सोना गिरवी रखने सहित 1991 के भुगतान संतुलन संकट को संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>सी. रंगराजन</b> उनके उत्तराधिकारी बने (1992–97)।<br>• <b>मनमोहन सिंह</b> 1982–85 में RBI गवर्नर और 1991 में वित्त मंत्री थे।<br>• <b>आई.जी. पटेल</b> 1977–82 में गवर्नर थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074525","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Literacy is considered essential for human development because it enables people to: [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"साक्षरता को मानव विकास के लिए आवश्यक माना जाता है क्योंकि यह लोगों को सक्षम बनाती है: [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Acquire industrial knowledge, skills, and awareness","hi":"औद्योगिक ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने में"},"2":{"en":"Acquire import related knowledge, skills, and awareness","hi":"आयात-संबंधी ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने में"},"3":{"en":"Acquire knowledge, skills, and awareness","hi":"ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने में"},"4":{"en":"Acquire taxation related knowledge, skills, and awareness","hi":"कराधान-संबंधी ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने में"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Acquire knowledge, skills, and awareness</b><br>Literacy helps people <b><u>acquire knowledge, skills and awareness</u></b> in general, which widens their choices and capabilities – the core idea of human development.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Education (\"knowledge\") is one of the <b>three dimensions</b> of HDI.<br>• India's literacy rate (Census 2011): <b>74.04%</b>; highest – <b>Kerala</b>, lowest – <b>Bihar</b>.<br>• <b>8 September</b> is International Literacy Day.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने में</b><br>साक्षरता लोगों को सामान्य रूप से <b><u>ज्ञान, कौशल और जागरूकता प्राप्त करने</u></b> में मदद करती है, जिससे उनके विकल्प और क्षमताएँ बढ़ती हैं – यही मानव विकास का मूल विचार है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शिक्षा (\"ज्ञान\") HDI के <b>तीन आयामों</b> में से एक है।<br>• भारत की साक्षरता दर (जनगणना 2011): <b>74.04%</b>; सर्वाधिक – <b>केरल</b>, न्यूनतम – <b>बिहार</b>।<br>• <b>8 सितंबर</b> अंतर्राष्ट्रीय साक्षरता दिवस है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074526","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which of the following is reflected in the knowledge dimension of the Human Development Index (HDI)? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) के ज्ञान आयाम में निम्नलिखित में से क्या परिलक्षित होता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Population growth","hi":"जनसंख्या वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Educational attainment","hi":"शैक्षिक उपलब्धि"},"3":{"en":"Internet connectivity only","hi":"केवल इंटरनेट कनेक्टिविटी"},"4":{"en":"Technological patents only","hi":"केवल तकनीकी पेटेंट"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Educational attainment</b><br>The knowledge dimension of HDI reflects <b><u>educational attainment</u></b>, measured by <b>mean years of schooling</b> (adults) and <b>expected years of schooling</b> (children).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other dimensions: <b>long and healthy life</b> and <b>decent standard of living</b> (GNI per capita).<br>• HDI is published by <b>UNDP</b> since <b>1990</b>.<br>• Adult literacy was dropped from HDI in <b>2010</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – शैक्षिक उपलब्धि</b><br>HDI का ज्ञान आयाम <b><u>शैक्षिक उपलब्धि</u></b> को दर्शाता है, जिसे <b>स्कूली शिक्षा के औसत वर्ष</b> (वयस्क) और <b>अपेक्षित वर्ष</b> (बच्चे) से मापा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अन्य आयाम: <b>दीर्घ और स्वस्थ जीवन</b> और <b>उचित जीवन स्तर</b> (प्रति व्यक्ति GNI)।<br>• HDI <b>1990</b> से <b>UNDP</b> द्वारा प्रकाशित।<br>• <b>2010</b> में वयस्क साक्षरता को HDI से हटाया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074527","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"What were the specific targeted growth rates for Real GDP and the agriculture sector established under the Twelfth Five-Year Plan (2012–2017)? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बारहवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2012–2017) के तहत वास्तविक GDP और कृषि क्षेत्र के लिए निर्धारित विशिष्ट लक्षित वृद्धि दरें क्या थीं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Real GDP: 9.0%, Agriculture: 3.7%","hi":"वास्तविक GDP: 9.0%, कृषि: 3.7%"},"2":{"en":"Real GDP: 8.0%, Agriculture: 4.0%","hi":"वास्तविक GDP: 8.0%, कृषि: 4.0%"},"3":{"en":"Real GDP: 7.6%, Agriculture: 4.5%","hi":"वास्तविक GDP: 7.6%, कृषि: 4.5%"},"4":{"en":"Real GDP: 6.5%, Agriculture: 3.5%","hi":"वास्तविक GDP: 6.5%, कृषि: 3.5%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Real GDP: 8.0%, Agriculture: 4.0%</b><br>The <b>Twelfth Plan</b> (\"Faster, More Inclusive and Sustainable Growth\") targeted <b><u>8% real GDP growth</u></b> (reduced from 9%) and <b><u>4% agriculture growth</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Manufacturing sector growth target: <b>10%</b>.<br>• It was the <b>last Five-Year Plan</b>; NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015.<br>• Eleventh Plan (2007–12) target: <b>9% GDP, 4% agriculture</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वास्तविक GDP: 8.0%, कृषि: 4.0%</b><br><b>बारहवीं योजना</b> (\"तीव्र, अधिक समावेशी और सतत विकास\") ने <b><u>8% वास्तविक GDP वृद्धि</u></b> (9% से घटाकर) और <b><u>4% कृषि वृद्धि</u></b> का लक्ष्य रखा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विनिर्माण क्षेत्र का वृद्धि लक्ष्य: <b>10%</b>।<br>• यह <b>अंतिम पंचवर्षीय योजना</b> थी; 2015 में नीति आयोग ने योजना आयोग का स्थान लिया।<br>• ग्यारहवीं योजना (2007–12) का लक्ष्य: <b>9% GDP, 4% कृषि</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074528","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Force and Laws of Motion","question":{"en":"A 2 kg block moving at 6 m/s collides head-on with a stationary 4 kg block. The two blocks stick together after the collision. Assuming no external horizontal force acts on the system, what fraction of the initial kinetic energy is lost? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"6 m/s से गतिमान 2 kg का एक ब्लॉक स्थिर 4 kg के ब्लॉक से आमने-सामने टकराता है। टक्कर के बाद दोनों ब्लॉक आपस में चिपक जाते हैं। यह मानते हुए कि तंत्र पर कोई बाहरी क्षैतिज बल नहीं लगता, प्रारंभिक गतिज ऊर्जा का कितना अंश नष्ट होता है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)</b><br>Momentum conservation: \\(2 \\times 6 = (2+4)v \\Rightarrow v = 2\\) m/s<br>Initial KE \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 6^2 = 36\\) J; Final KE \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 2^2 = 12\\) J<br>Fraction lost \\(= \\frac{36 - 12}{36} = \\frac{2}{3}\\) = <b><u>\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• When bodies stick together, the collision is <b>perfectly inelastic</b> – maximum KE loss.<br>• In all collisions, <b>linear momentum is conserved</b>; KE is conserved only in elastic collisions.<br>• Lost KE converts into heat, sound and deformation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)</b><br>संवेग संरक्षण: \\(2 \\times 6 = (2+4)v \\Rightarrow v = 2\\) m/s<br>प्रारंभिक गतिज ऊर्जा \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 6^2 = 36\\) J; अंतिम गतिज ऊर्जा \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 2^2 = 12\\) J<br>नष्ट अंश \\(= \\frac{36 - 12}{36} = \\frac{2}{3}\\) = <b><u>\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जब वस्तुएँ आपस में चिपक जाती हैं, तो टक्कर <b>पूर्णतः अप्रत्यास्थ</b> होती है – अधिकतम गतिज ऊर्जा हानि।<br>• सभी टक्करों में <b>रैखिक संवेग संरक्षित</b> रहता है; गतिज ऊर्जा केवल प्रत्यास्थ टक्कर में संरक्षित रहती है।<br>• नष्ट गतिज ऊर्जा ऊष्मा, ध्वनि और विरूपण में बदलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074529","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Indian National Congress","question":{"en":"Under whose leadership was Purna Swaraj formally adopted at the Lahore Session? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लाहौर अधिवेशन में पूर्ण स्वराज किसके नेतृत्व में औपचारिक रूप से अपनाया गया? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Subhas Chandra Bose","hi":"सुभाष चंद्र बोस"},"2":{"en":"Rajendra Prasad","hi":"राजेंद्र प्रसाद"},"3":{"en":"Jawaharlal Nehru","hi":"जवाहरलाल नेहरू"},"4":{"en":"Vallabhbhai Patel","hi":"वल्लभभाई पटेल"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Jawaharlal Nehru</b><br>The <b>Lahore Session of INC (December 1929)</b>, presided over by <b><u>Jawaharlal Nehru</u></b>, adopted the <b>Purna Swaraj</b> resolution; Nehru hoisted the tricolour on the bank of the Ravi on 31 December 1929.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>26 January 1930</b> was celebrated as the first <b>Independence Day</b>.<br>• The session authorised the <b>Civil Disobedience Movement</b>.<br>• This is why the Constitution came into force on <b>26 January 1950</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जवाहरलाल नेहरू</b><br><b><u>जवाहरलाल नेहरू</u></b> की अध्यक्षता में <b>कांग्रेस के लाहौर अधिवेशन (दिसंबर 1929)</b> में <b>पूर्ण स्वराज</b> प्रस्ताव पारित हुआ; नेहरू ने 31 दिसंबर 1929 को रावी तट पर तिरंगा फहराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>26 जनवरी 1930</b> को पहला <b>स्वतंत्रता दिवस</b> मनाया गया।<br>• अधिवेशन ने <b>सविनय अवज्ञा आंदोलन</b> की अनुमति दी।<br>• इसी कारण संविधान <b>26 जनवरी 1950</b> को लागू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074530","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Digestion and Respiration","question":{"en":"A person has difficulty digesting fats because bile is not being produced properly. Which organ is most likely affected? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति को वसा पचाने में कठिनाई होती है क्योंकि पित्त ठीक से नहीं बन रहा है। कौन-सा अंग सबसे अधिक प्रभावित होने की संभावना है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Heart","hi":"हृदय"},"2":{"en":"Liver","hi":"यकृत"},"3":{"en":"Kidney","hi":"गुर्दा"},"4":{"en":"Lungs","hi":"फेफड़े"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Liver</b><br><b>Bile</b> is produced by the <b><u>liver</u></b> and stored in the gall bladder. Bile salts <b>emulsify fats</b> into tiny droplets so lipase can digest them.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The liver is the <b>largest gland</b> of the human body.<br>• Bile contains <b>no digestive enzyme</b>; it makes the medium alkaline.<br>• Fats are finally digested by <b>pancreatic lipase</b> into fatty acids and glycerol.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – यकृत</b><br><b>पित्त</b> <b><u>यकृत (Liver)</u></b> द्वारा बनता है और पित्ताशय में संग्रहीत होता है। पित्त लवण <b>वसा का पायसीकरण</b> करके उसे छोटी बूँदों में बदलते हैं, ताकि लाइपेज़ उसे पचा सके।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यकृत मानव शरीर की <b>सबसे बड़ी ग्रंथि</b> है।<br>• पित्त में <b>कोई पाचक एंज़ाइम नहीं</b> होता; यह माध्यम को क्षारीय बनाता है।<br>• वसा अंततः <b>अग्नाशयी लाइपेज़</b> द्वारा वसीय अम्ल और ग्लिसरॉल में पचती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074531","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a hexagonal base with an area of 90 cm². The height of the prism is 20 cm. Find the volume. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का षट्कोणीय आधार है जिसका क्षेत्रफल 90 cm² है। प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 20 cm है। आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1800 cm³"},"2":{"en":"2000 cm³"},"3":{"en":"2200 cm³"},"4":{"en":"2500 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"180\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-25 0 180 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M129 39L123 26M129 183L129 39M123 26L72 26M72 26L26 39M26 183L32 196M26 39L32 52M26 183L26 39M32 196L83 196M32 52L83 52M32 196L32 52M83 196L129 183M83 52L129 39M83 196L83 52\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M129 183L123 170M123 170L72 170M123 170L123 26M72 170L26 183M72 170L72 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"-2\" y=\"115\">20 cm</text></g></svg><br>Volume of a prism \\(= \\) base area \\(\\times\\) height<br>\\(V = 90 \\times 20 = \\boxed{1800\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1800 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"180\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-25 0 180 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M129 39L123 26M129 183L129 39M123 26L72 26M72 26L26 39M26 183L32 196M26 39L32 52M26 183L26 39M32 196L83 196M32 52L83 52M32 196L32 52M83 196L129 183M83 52L129 39M83 196L83 52\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M129 183L123 170M123 170L72 170M123 170L123 26M72 170L26 183M72 170L72 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"-2\" y=\"115\">20 cm</text></g></svg><br>प्रिज़्म का आयतन \\(= \\) आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(\\times\\) ऊँचाई<br>\\(V = 90 \\times 20 = \\boxed{1800\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1800 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074532","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the expression: \\(\\sqrt{0.25} + \\sqrt{0.36} + \\sqrt{1.44} + \\sqrt{0.0009}\\). [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्यंजक को सरल कीजिए: \\(\\sqrt{0.25} + \\sqrt{0.36} + \\sqrt{1.44} + \\sqrt{0.0009}\\)। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.33"},"2":{"en":"1.67"},"3":{"en":"4.71"},"4":{"en":"3.19"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{0.25} = 0.5\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.36} = 0.6\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.44} = 1.2\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0009} = 0.03\\)<br>Sum \\(= 0.5 + 0.6 + 1.2 + 0.03 = \\boxed{2.33}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.33.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{0.25} = 0.5\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.36} = 0.6\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.44} = 1.2\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0009} = 0.03\\)<br>योग \\(= 0.5 + 0.6 + 1.2 + 0.03 = \\boxed{2.33}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2.33 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074533","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a triangle, the centroid divides each median in the ratio 2:1. What is the distance between the centroid and the orthocenter in an equilateral triangle? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज में केंद्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2:1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है। एक समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक और लंबकेंद्र के बीच की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Equal to the side length","hi":"भुजा की लंबाई के बराबर"},"2":{"en":"Zero","hi":"शून्य"},"3":{"en":"Half the side length","hi":"भुजा की लंबाई की आधी"},"4":{"en":"One-third of the side length","hi":"भुजा की लंबाई की एक-तिहाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle the centroid, orthocenter, circumcentre and incentre all coincide<br>So the distance between centroid and orthocenter \\(= \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Zero.</b>","hi":"समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक, लंबकेंद्र, परिकेंद्र और अंतःकेंद्र सभी एक ही बिंदु पर होते हैं<br>अतः केंद्रक और लंबकेंद्र के बीच दूरी \\(= \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): शून्य है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074534","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"Find the least perfect square divisible by 3, 4, 5, 6, and 8. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"3, 4, 5, 6 और 8 से विभाज्य न्यूनतम पूर्ण वर्ग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3800"},"2":{"en":"3600"},"3":{"en":"4600"},"4":{"en":"4200"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\text{LCM}(3,4,5,6,8) = 120 = 2^3 \\times 3 \\times 5\\)<br>To make it a perfect square multiply by \\(2 \\times 3 \\times 5 = 30\\)<br>\\(120 \\times 30 = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3600.</b>","hi":"\\(\\text{LCM}(3,4,5,6,8) = 120 = 2^3 \\times 3 \\times 5\\)<br>पूर्ण वर्ग बनाने के लिए \\(2 \\times 3 \\times 5 = 30\\) से गुणा कीजिए<br>\\(120 \\times 30 = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074535","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B started a business with capital in the ratio 5 : 9. At the end of 8 months, A withdrew his capital. If they receive profits in the ratio 4 : 9, for how many months was B's capital used in the business? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B ने 5 : 9 के अनुपात में पूँजी लगाकर व्यवसाय शुरू किया। 8 माह के अंत में A ने अपनी पूँजी निकाल ली। यदि उन्हें लाभ 4 : 9 के अनुपात में मिलता है, तो B की पूँजी कितने माह तक व्यवसाय में लगी रही? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 months","hi":"6 माह"},"2":{"en":"9 months","hi":"9 माह"},"3":{"en":"12 months","hi":"12 माह"},"4":{"en":"10 months","hi":"10 माह"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Profit ratio \\(= \\) capital \\(\\times\\) time<br>\\(\\frac{5 \\times 8}{9 \\times t} = \\frac{4}{9} \\Rightarrow \\frac{40}{9t} = \\frac{4}{9}\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{10\\ \\text{months}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10 months.</b>","hi":"लाभ अनुपात \\(= \\) पूँजी \\(\\times\\) समय<br>\\(\\frac{5 \\times 8}{9 \\times t} = \\frac{4}{9} \\Rightarrow \\frac{40}{9t} = \\frac{4}{9}\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{10\\ \\text{माह}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 माह है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074536","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum becomes 9 times its original value in 4 years under compound interest. In how many years will it become 81 times the original amount? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कोई धनराशि चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर 4 वर्ष में अपने मूल मान का 9 गुना हो जाती है। कितने वर्षों में वह मूल राशि का 81 गुना हो जाएगी? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 years","hi":"8 वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"7 years","hi":"7 वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"5 years","hi":"5 वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"6 years","hi":"6 वर्ष"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((1 + r)^4 = 9\\); \\(81 = 9^2\\)<br>\\((1 + r)^{8} = 9^2 = 81\\)<br>Time \\(= \\boxed{8\\ \\text{years}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8 years.</b>","hi":"\\((1 + r)^4 = 9\\); \\(81 = 9^2\\)<br>\\((1 + r)^{8} = 9^2 = 81\\)<br>समय \\(= \\boxed{8\\ \\text{वर्ष}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 वर्ष है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074537","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A floor is covered by regular hexagonal tiles of side 12 cm. If 5% are broken during installation, and total area to be covered is 12 m², approximately how many tiles are needed? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक फर्श पर 12 cm भुजा वाली सम षट्कोणीय टाइलें लगाई जाती हैं। यदि लगाने के दौरान 5% टूट जाती हैं और कुल ढकने वाला क्षेत्रफल 12 m² है, तो लगभग कितनी टाइलें आवश्यक हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"343 tiles","hi":"343 टाइल"},"2":{"en":"338 tiles","hi":"338 टाइल"},"3":{"en":"318 tiles","hi":"318 टाइल"},"4":{"en":"323 tiles","hi":"323 टाइल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Area of one tile \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}(12)^2 = 216\\sqrt{3} \\approx 374.1\\ \\text{cm}^2\\)<br>Tiles needed \\(= \\frac{120000}{374.1} \\approx 320.8\\)<br>With 5% breakage \\(= 320.8 \\times 1.05 \\approx \\boxed{338}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 338 tiles.</b>","hi":"एक टाइल का क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}(12)^2 = 216\\sqrt{3} \\approx 374.1\\ \\text{cm}^2\\)<br>आवश्यक टाइलें \\(= \\frac{120000}{374.1} \\approx 320.8\\)<br>5% टूटने के साथ \\(= 320.8 \\times 1.05 \\approx \\boxed{338}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 338 टाइल है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074538","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a quadrant of a circle is \\(\\frac{49\\pi}{4}\\) cm². What is the radius of the circle? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त के चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल \\(\\frac{49\\pi}{4}\\) cm² है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9 cm"},"2":{"en":"4 cm"},"3":{"en":"7 cm"},"4":{"en":"6 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M176 176L26 176L26 26M176 176A150 150 0 0 0 26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"192\">r</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"105\">r</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">O</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\pi r^2 = \\frac{49\\pi}{4}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 49\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{7\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 7 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M176 176L26 176L26 26M176 176A150 150 0 0 0 26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"192\">r</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"105\">r</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">O</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\pi r^2 = \\frac{49\\pi}{4}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 49\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{7\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 7 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074539","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone has a volume of 450π cm³ and a height of 6 cm. Find the radius of its base. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक शंकु का आयतन 450π cm³ और ऊँचाई 6 cm है। उसके आधार की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 cm"},"2":{"en":"13 cm"},"3":{"en":"19 cm"},"4":{"en":"18 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"106\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 106\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 56A75 24 0 0 0 176 56M26 56L101 26L176 56M107 56L107 50L101 50\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 56A75 24 0 0 1 176 56M101 26L101 56M101 56L176 56\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"56\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">6 cm</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"11\">r</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 450\\pi\\)<br>\\(r^2 = \\frac{450 \\times 3}{6} = 225\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{15\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"106\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 106\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 56A75 24 0 0 0 176 56M26 56L101 26L176 56M107 56L107 50L101 50\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 56A75 24 0 0 1 176 56M101 26L101 56M101 56L176 56\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"56\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">6 cm</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"11\">r</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 450\\pi\\)<br>\\(r^2 = \\frac{450 \\times 3}{6} = 225\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{15\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074540","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"An item is sold by a manufacturer to a wholesaler at a profit of 10%. Then it is sold by the wholesaler to a retailer at a profit of 20%. The retailer again sells the item to a customer for ₹56,100 at a loss of 15%. Find the cost price of the item to the manufacturer. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निर्माता कोई वस्तु थोक व्यापारी को 10% लाभ पर बेचता है। फिर थोक व्यापारी उसे खुदरा व्यापारी को 20% लाभ पर बेचता है। खुदरा व्यापारी वह वस्तु ग्राहक को ₹56,100 में 15% हानि पर बेचता है। निर्माता के लिए उस वस्तु का क्रय मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹60,000"},"2":{"en":"₹70,000"},"3":{"en":"₹50,000"},"4":{"en":"₹80,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the manufacturer's cost be \\(x\\)<br>\\(x \\times 1.1 \\times 1.2 \\times 0.85 = 56100\\)<br>\\(x \\times 1.122 = 56100 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{50{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹50,000.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए निर्माता का क्रय मूल्य \\(x\\) है<br>\\(x \\times 1.1 \\times 1.2 \\times 0.85 = 56100\\)<br>\\(x \\times 1.122 = 56100 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{50{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹50,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074541","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A wholesaler allows a discount of 20% on the marked price to a retailer. The retailer sells the item at a 5% discount on the marked price. If the retailer uses a faulty weight that weighs 900g for every 1kg while selling, what is his overall approximate profit percentage? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक थोक व्यापारी खुदरा व्यापारी को अंकित मूल्य पर 20% छूट देता है। खुदरा व्यापारी वह वस्तु अंकित मूल्य पर 5% छूट पर बेचता है। यदि खुदरा व्यापारी बेचते समय ऐसे त्रुटिपूर्ण बाट का उपयोग करता है जो प्रत्येक 1kg के लिए 900g तौलता है, तो उसका कुल अनुमानित लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42%"},"2":{"en":"56%"},"3":{"en":"74%"},"4":{"en":"32%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let MP \\(= 100\\); retailer's CP \\(= 80\\)<br>He collects 95 for only 900 g, i.e. cost of goods sold \\(= 80 \\times 0.9 = 72\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\frac{95 - 72}{72} \\times 100 \\approx \\boxed{32\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 32%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए अंकित मूल्य \\(= 100\\); खुदरा व्यापारी का क्रय मूल्य \\(= 80\\)<br>वह केवल 900 g के लिए 95 वसूलता है, अर्थात बेचे गए माल की लागत \\(= 80 \\times 0.9 = 72\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\frac{95 - 72}{72} \\times 100 \\approx \\boxed{32\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 32% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074542","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A man standing on a tower observes a car approaching him. The angle of depression changes from 30° to 60° in 8 minutes. Find the time taken by the car to reach the tower from that position. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक मीनार पर खड़ा व्यक्ति अपनी ओर आती हुई एक कार को देखता है। अवनमन कोण 8 मिनट में 30° से 60° हो जाता है। उस स्थिति से मीनार तक पहुँचने में कार द्वारा लिया गया समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 mins","hi":"5 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"4 mins","hi":"4 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"2 mins","hi":"2 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"6 mins","hi":"6 मिनट"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M103 159L26 26M48 26A22 22 0 0 1 37 45M256 159L26 26M72 26A46 46 0 0 1 66 49\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 26L256 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"173\">Q</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">P</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"175\">8 min</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"175\">?</text></g></svg><br>At 30°: distance \\(= h\\sqrt{3}\\); at 60°: distance \\(= \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>Covered \\(= h\\sqrt{3} - \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) in 8 min<br>Remaining \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) is half of that \\(\\Rightarrow \\boxed{4\\ \\text{mins}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4 mins.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M103 159L26 26M48 26A22 22 0 0 1 37 45M256 159L26 26M72 26A46 46 0 0 1 66 49\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 26L256 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"173\">Q</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">P</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"175\">8 min</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"175\">?</text></g></svg><br>30° पर: दूरी \\(= h\\sqrt{3}\\); 60° पर: दूरी \\(= \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>तय की गई \\(= h\\sqrt{3} - \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), 8 मिनट में<br>शेष \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) उसका आधा है \\(\\Rightarrow \\boxed{4\\ \\text{मिनट}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074543","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The measure of supplement of ∠y is 40° more than twice the measure of the complement of ∠y. Find the sum in degrees of the supplement and complement of ∠y. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"∠y के संपूरक का माप, ∠y के पूरक के माप के दुगुने से 40° अधिक है। ∠y के संपूरक और पूरक के मापों का योग (डिग्री में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"270°"},"2":{"en":"150°"},"3":{"en":"190°"},"4":{"en":"110°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(180 - y = 2(90 - y) + 40 = 220 - 2y\\)<br>\\(y = 40°\\)<br>Supplement \\(= 140°\\), complement \\(= 50°\\); sum \\(= \\boxed{190°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 190°.</b>","hi":"\\(180 - y = 2(90 - y) + 40 = 220 - 2y\\)<br>\\(y = 40°\\)<br>संपूरक \\(= 140°\\), पूरक \\(= 50°\\); योग \\(= \\boxed{190°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 190° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074544","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If 0° < θ < 90°, find the value of \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}} - \\tan\\theta\\). [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 0° < θ < 90° है, तो \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}} - \\tan\\theta\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"sinθ"},"2":{"en":"cosθ"},"3":{"en":"secθ"},"4":{"en":"tanθ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\sin\\theta)^2}{1-\\sin^2\\theta}} = \\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\)<br>So the expression \\(= \\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta - \\tan\\theta = \\boxed{\\sec\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): secθ.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\sin\\theta)^2}{1-\\sin^2\\theta}} = \\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\)<br>अतः व्यंजक \\(= \\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta - \\tan\\theta = \\boxed{\\sec\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): secθ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074545","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{5}\\sin\\theta = 1\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{2\\tan\\theta + \\sqrt{5}\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{5}\\cos\\theta - 2\\tan\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{5}\\sin\\theta = 1\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{2\\tan\\theta + \\sqrt{5}\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{5}\\cos\\theta - 2\\tan\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\), \\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>Numerator \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) + 1 = 2\\); denominator \\(= 2 - 1 = 1\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2}{1} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\), \\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>अंश \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) + 1 = 2\\); हर \\(= 2 - 1 = 1\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2}{1} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074546","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid metallic cone of radius 6 cm and height 12 cm is melted and recast into small solid spheres of radius 1 cm. How many such spheres can be made? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"6 cm त्रिज्या और 12 cm ऊँचाई वाले एक ठोस धात्विक शंकु को पिघलाकर 1 cm त्रिज्या के छोटे ठोस गोले बनाए जाते हैं। ऐसे कितने गोले बनाए जा सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"86"},"2":{"en":"93"},"3":{"en":"102"},"4":{"en":"108"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Cone volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (36)(12) = 144\\pi\\)<br>Sphere volume \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (1)^3 = \\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\)<br>Number \\(= \\frac{144\\pi}{4\\pi/3} = \\boxed{108}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 108.</b>","hi":"शंकु का आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (36)(12) = 144\\pi\\)<br>गोले का आयतन \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (1)^3 = \\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\)<br>संख्या \\(= \\frac{144\\pi}{4\\pi/3} = \\boxed{108}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 108 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074547","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, points D and E lie on sides AB and AC, respectively, such that DE is parallel to BC. If AD : DB = 2 : 3 and AE = 8 cm, then find the length of AC. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D और E क्रमशः भुजाओं AB और AC पर इस प्रकार हैं कि DE, BC के समांतर है। यदि AD : DB = 2 : 3 और AE = 8 cm है, तो AC की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 cm"},"2":{"en":"18 cm"},"3":{"en":"20 cm"},"4":{"en":"24 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM67 94L148 94\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"98\">D</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"98\">E</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"59\">2</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"144\">3</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"56\">8</text></g></svg><br>\\(DE \\parallel BC \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{8}{AC}\\)<br>\\(AC = \\boxed{20\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 20 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM67 94L148 94\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"98\">D</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"98\">E</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"59\">2</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"144\">3</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"56\">8</text></g></svg><br>\\(DE \\parallel BC \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{8}{AC}\\)<br>\\(AC = \\boxed{20\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 20 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074548","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A farmer borrowed ₹2,50,000 at simple interest under a rural credit scheme. After 7 years, he repaid ₹3,72,500. If another farmer borrowed ₹4,00,000 at the same rate but for 10 years, how much more interest would the second farmer pay than that paid by the first farmer? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक किसान ने ग्रामीण ऋण योजना के अंतर्गत साधारण ब्याज पर ₹2,50,000 उधार लिए। 7 वर्ष बाद उसने ₹3,72,500 चुकाए। यदि दूसरा किसान उसी दर पर ₹4,00,000, 10 वर्ष के लिए उधार लेता है, तो दूसरा किसान पहले किसान से कितना अधिक ब्याज देगा? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,50,900"},"2":{"en":"₹1,51,000"},"3":{"en":"₹1,55,200"},"4":{"en":"₹1,57,500"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Interest 1 \\(= 372500 - 250000 = 122500\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{122500 \\times 100}{250000 \\times 7} = 7\\%\\)<br>Interest 2 \\(= \\frac{400000 \\times 7 \\times 10}{100} = 280000\\)<br>Difference \\(= 280000 - 122500 = \\boxed{1{,}57{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹1,57,500.</b>","hi":"ब्याज 1 \\(= 372500 - 250000 = 122500\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{122500 \\times 100}{250000 \\times 7} = 7\\%\\)<br>ब्याज 2 \\(= \\frac{400000 \\times 7 \\times 10}{100} = 280000\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 280000 - 122500 = \\boxed{1{,}57{,}500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹1,57,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074549","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A commercial property needs painting. 60% of the total surface area consists of walls and 40% consists of ceilings. Painter E can paint all the walls in 6 hours but would take 12 hours to paint the ceilings. Painter F can paint all the ceilings alone in 4 hours, but the walls alone would take her 18 hours. They start working simultaneously, splitting the tasks optimally based on their respective speeds. The moment either painter finishes their initial assignment, they immediately join the other to help finish the remaining surface. How long will it take them to paint the entire property? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वाणिज्यिक संपत्ति को रंगना है। कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल का 60% दीवारें और 40% छतें हैं। पेंटर E सभी दीवारों को 6 घंटे में रंग सकता है, परंतु छतों को रंगने में उसे 12 घंटे लगेंगे। पेंटर F अकेली सभी छतों को 4 घंटे में रंग सकती है, परंतु अकेली दीवारों पर उसे 18 घंटे लगेंगे। वे अपनी-अपनी गति के आधार पर कार्य को इष्टतम रूप से बाँटकर एक साथ काम शुरू करते हैं। जैसे ही कोई पेंटर अपना प्रारंभिक कार्य पूरा करता/करती है, वह तुरंत दूसरे की सहायता करने लगता/लगती है। पूरी संपत्ति रंगने में उन्हें कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5.5 hrs","hi":"5.5 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"6 hrs","hi":"6 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"6.4 hrs","hi":"6.4 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"8 hrs","hi":"8 घंटे"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"E is faster at walls, F at ceilings, so E takes walls (60%) and F takes ceilings (40%)<br>E's wall rate \\(= 10\\%\\) per hour, F's ceiling rate \\(= 10\\%\\) per hour<br>In 4 hours F finishes ceilings; E does 40% of walls, 20% remains<br>Together on walls: \\(10\\% + \\frac{60}{18}\\% \\approx 13.33\\%\\) per hour \\(\\Rightarrow 1.5\\) h<br>Total \\(= 4 + 1.5 = \\boxed{5.5\\ \\text{hrs}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5.5 hrs.</b>","hi":"E दीवारों में तेज़ है, F छतों में, अतः E दीवारें (60%) और F छतें (40%) लेती है<br>E की दीवार गति \\(= 10\\%\\) प्रति घंटा, F की छत गति \\(= 10\\%\\) प्रति घंटा<br>4 घंटे में F छतें पूरी करती है; E दीवारों का 40% करता है, 20% शेष<br>दीवारों पर साथ: \\(10\\% + \\frac{60}{18}\\% \\approx 13.33\\%\\) प्रति घंटा \\(\\Rightarrow 1.5\\) घंटे<br>कुल \\(= 4 + 1.5 = \\boxed{5.5\\ \\text{घंटे}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5.5 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074550","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Two software engineers, Naina and Kapil, are debugging a block of code. Working independently, Naina can clear 10% of the code per hour and Kapil can clear 8% per hour. However, when working together in the same virtual environment, the communication overhead reduces each of their individual efficiencies by exactly 10%. If they work together for 2 hours after which Kapil leaves, how much more time will it take Naina so that a total of 40% of the block of code gets debugged? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो सॉफ़्टवेयर इंजीनियर, नैना और कपिल, कोड के एक ब्लॉक को डीबग कर रहे हैं। अलग-अलग काम करते हुए नैना प्रति घंटा कोड का 10% और कपिल प्रति घंटा 8% साफ़ कर सकता है। परंतु एक ही वर्चुअल वातावरण में साथ काम करते समय संचार ओवरहेड उनकी व्यक्तिगत क्षमता को ठीक 10% कम कर देता है। यदि वे 2 घंटे साथ काम करते हैं और फिर कपिल चला जाता है, तो कोड के ब्लॉक का कुल 40% डीबग करने के लिए नैना को और कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40 mins","hi":"40 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"42.8 mins","hi":"42.8 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"44.5 mins","hi":"44.5 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"45.6 mins","hi":"45.6 मिनट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Together: Naina \\(9\\%\\)/h, Kapil \\(7.2\\%\\)/h \\(\\Rightarrow 16.2\\%\\)/h<br>In 2 hours \\(= 32.4\\%\\); remaining \\(= 7.6\\%\\)<br>Naina alone: \\(\\frac{7.6}{10}\\) h \\(= 0.76 \\times 60 = \\boxed{45.6\\ \\text{mins}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 45.6 mins.</b>","hi":"साथ में: नैना \\(9\\%\\)/घंटा, कपिल \\(7.2\\%\\)/घंटा \\(\\Rightarrow 16.2\\%\\)/घंटा<br>2 घंटे में \\(= 32.4\\%\\); शेष \\(= 7.6\\%\\)<br>नैना अकेली: \\(\\frac{7.6}{10}\\) घंटा \\(= 0.76 \\times 60 = \\boxed{45.6\\ \\text{मिनट}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 45.6 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074551","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\frac{\\sec 73°}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\,17°} - 1\\) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sec 73°}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\,17°} - 1\\) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"−1"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\,17° = \\sec(90° - 17°) = \\sec 73°\\)<br>So the fraction \\(= 1\\)<br>\\(1 - 1 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.</b>","hi":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\,17° = \\sec(90° - 17°) = \\sec 73°\\)<br>अतः भिन्न \\(= 1\\)<br>\\(1 - 1 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074552","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If x = 109 and y = 98, evaluate the expression x² - y² + 2x - 2y without using direct multiplication. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि x = 109 और y = 98 है, तो सीधे गुणा किए बिना व्यंजक x² - y² + 2x - 2y का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1089"},"2":{"en":"1386"},"3":{"en":"2299"},"4":{"en":"2357"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 - y^2 + 2x - 2y = (x - y)(x + y) + 2(x - y)\\)<br>\\(= (x - y)(x + y + 2) = 11 \\times 209\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2299}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2299.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 - y^2 + 2x - 2y = (x - y)(x + y) + 2(x - y)\\)<br>\\(= (x - y)(x + y + 2) = 11 \\times 209\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2299}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2299 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074553","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(p + q + r = 0\\) and \\(pq + qr + rp = -18\\), then find the value of \\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2\\). [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(p + q + r = 0\\) और \\(pq + qr + rp = -18\\) है, तो \\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"−18"},"2":{"en":"−36"},"3":{"en":"0"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = (p + q + r)^2 - 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(= 0 - 2(-18)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 36.</b>","hi":"\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = (p + q + r)^2 - 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(= 0 - 2(-18)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 36 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074554","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A swimming pool is designed with a regular octagonal floor plan of side length 20 m. The floor of the pool is to be tiled using tiles that cover 0.25 m² each. Assuming no material is wasted during cutting, find the total number of tiles required (approximately). [Take √2 ≈ 1.4142] [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक स्विमिंग पूल 20 m भुजा वाले सम अष्टभुजाकार फर्श के साथ बनाया गया है। पूल का फर्श 0.25 m² क्षेत्रफल वाली टाइलों से बनाया जाना है। यह मानते हुए कि काटने में कोई सामग्री बर्बाद नहीं होती, आवश्यक टाइलों की कुल संख्या (लगभग) ज्ञात कीजिए। [√2 ≈ 1.4142 लीजिए] [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6534"},"2":{"en":"7999"},"3":{"en":"7726"},"4":{"en":"7000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Area of regular octagon \\(= 2(1 + \\sqrt{2})a^2\\)<br>\\(= 2(2.4142)(400) \\approx 1931.4\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>Tiles \\(= \\frac{1931.4}{0.25} \\approx \\boxed{7726}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 7726.</b>","hi":"सम अष्टभुज का क्षेत्रफल \\(= 2(1 + \\sqrt{2})a^2\\)<br>\\(= 2(2.4142)(400) \\approx 1931.4\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>टाइलें \\(= \\frac{1931.4}{0.25} \\approx \\boxed{7726}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 7726 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074555","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression: \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}+1}\\) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}+1}\\) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2}{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}+1} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Sum \\(= (2 + \\sqrt{3}) + (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{3}+1)^2}{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}+1} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>योग \\(= (2 + \\sqrt{3}) + (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074556","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct direct speech transformation of the sentence below.<br>The banner welcomed visitors to Belgium. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The banner said, “Welcome to Belgium.”"},"2":{"en":"The banner said, “People, welcome to Belgium.”"},"3":{"en":"The banner said, “Belgium welcomes you.”"},"4":{"en":"The banner said, “Welcome Belgium.”"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A message on a banner can be reported as “The banner said,” followed by its direct wording.</b><br>“Welcome to Belgium” is the standard greeting to visitors.<br>B adds the unnecessary vocative “People”; C changes the sentence into a statement about Belgium.<br>D omits the preposition “to,” producing an incorrect greeting.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The banner said, “Welcome to Belgium.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074557","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The global push for sustainability<br>P. necessitating urgent collaboration among nations<br>Q. has been intensified by alarming environmental shifts,<br>R. and fostering the transition towards renewable energy sources<br>S. leading to policy frameworks aimed at reducing carbon emissions [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSPQ"},"2":{"en":"QPSR"},"3":{"en":"PSRQ"},"4":{"en":"SPRQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPSR</b><br>Q supplies the finite predicate “has been intensified by alarming environmental shifts.”<br>P adds its consequence: urgent collaboration among nations.<br>S describes resulting policy frameworks, and R adds the parallel result of fostering renewable energy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QPSR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074558","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>Jatin was progressing <b>by leaps and bounds</b> because of his hard work. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Very slowly"},"2":{"en":"With great speed and progress"},"3":{"en":"Without making any progress"},"4":{"en":"In a confused and disorganized manner"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>By leaps and bounds (बहुत तेजी से) = progressing very quickly.</b><br>Example: “Her language skills improved by leaps and bounds.”<br>“Very slowly” and “without making any progress” contradict the idiom.<br>It describes rapid progress, not confusion or disorganization.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): With great speed and progress.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074559","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>We were leave for the airport when the storm began. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"storm"},"2":{"en":"began"},"3":{"en":"airport"},"4":{"en":"leave"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past continuous = was/were + verb-ing.</b><br>After “were,” the verb must be “leaving,” not the base form “leave.”<br>Correct sentence: “We were <b>leaving</b> for the airport when the storm began.”<br>“Storm,” “began” and “airport” are correctly used.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): leave.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074560","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the sentence by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br>Were he to have followed the instructions, none of this ___ occurred. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"would have"},"2":{"en":"will have"},"3":{"en":"had"},"4":{"en":"should"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unreal past condition takes “would have + past participle” in the result clause.</b><br>“Were he to have followed” is an inverted hypothetical condition.<br>Completed sentence: “Were he to have followed the instructions, none of this <b>would have</b> occurred.”<br>“Will have” is not hypothetical; “had” and “should” do not form the required result construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): would have.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074561","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Their research revealed that fungi play a crucial role in nutrient cycling, breaking down organic matter and forming symbiotic relationships with plant roots.<br>2. Understanding these fungal connections has transformed ecological studies and highlights the interdependence of forest ecosystems.<br>3. In recent years, scientists have discovered vast underground fungal networks known as mycorrhizal networks.<br>4. These networks allow trees and plants to share nutrients and even send chemical signals, sometimes described as the “Wood Wide Web.”<br>5. Some species of fungi can even warn trees about insect attacks by transmitting distress signals through the underground network. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-5-1-3"},"2":{"en":"3-1-4-5-2"},"3":{"en":"1-4-3-5-2"},"4":{"en":"5-3-2-1-4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 3-1-4-5-2</b><br>Sentence 3 introduces the discovery of mycorrhizal networks, and sentence 1 explains the research findings.<br>Sentence 4 describes what “these networks” do; sentence 5 adds their warning function.<br>Sentence 2 concludes with the wider significance of understanding these connections.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3-1-4-5-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074562","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence using the correct phrasal verb of the underlined word.<br>The project was <u>given away</u> by the new manager after the old one retired. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"carried out"},"2":{"en":"carried away"},"3":{"en":"carried through"},"4":{"en":"carried in"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Carry out (कार्यान्वित करना) = perform, conduct or execute a task or project.</b><br>Correct sentence: “The project was <b>carried out</b> by the new manager after the old one retired.”<br><b>Carry away (बहक जाना)</b> = fill with emotion or remove<br><b>Carry through (पूरा करना)</b> = complete despite difficulty; <b>carry in (अंदर लाना)</b> = bring inside<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): carried out.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074563","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Internecine</b> [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Internal"},"2":{"en":"External"},"3":{"en":"Harmonious"},"4":{"en":"Civil"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Internecine (पारस्परिक विनाशकारी) = destructive to both sides within a group.</b><br><b>Internal (आंतरिक)</b> = situated within<br><b>External (बाहरी)</b> = situated outside<br><b>Harmonious (सामंजस्यपूर्ण)</b> = free from conflict ✔<br><b>Civil (नागरिक/विनम्र)</b> = relating to citizens or polite<br>More antonyms: peaceful, amicable, concordant.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Harmonious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074564","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>To milk the ram [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To exploit one's privilege"},"2":{"en":"To attempt the impossible or futile"},"3":{"en":"To exaggerate defeat"},"4":{"en":"To question authority subtly"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>To milk the ram (असंभव या व्यर्थ कार्य करना)</b><br>A ram is male and cannot give milk, so the idiom means attempting something impossible or pointless.<br>Example: “Arguing with him is like milking the ram.”<br>Exploiting privilege, exaggerating defeat and questioning authority do not convey futility.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To attempt the impossible or futile.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074565","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a cross-sensory phenomenon. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Synesthesia"},"2":{"en":"Synesthasia"},"3":{"en":"Synaesthesia"},"4":{"en":"Synestesia"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Synesthesia (संवेदन-संयोजन) = a condition in which one sense involuntarily stimulates another.</b><br>The American spelling “synesthesia” is correct.<br><b>Synesthasia</b> wrongly inserts “h” after “t”; <b>Synaesthesia</b> is the British variant, not the requested option here.<br><b>Synestesia</b> omits “h” from “-thes-.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Synesthesia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074566","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Inability to sleep.” [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Narcolepsy"},"2":{"en":"Insomnia"},"3":{"en":"Somnolence"},"4":{"en":"Somnambulist"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Insomnia (अनिद्रा) = persistent inability to fall or remain asleep.</b><br><b>Narcolepsy (निद्राघात)</b> = a disorder causing sudden sleep attacks<br><b>Somnolence (उनींदापन)</b> = drowsiness<br><b>Somnambulist (नींद में चलने वाला)</b> = a sleepwalker<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Insomnia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074567","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Looking or sounding sad and dismal.” [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jubiliant"},"2":{"en":"Lugubrious"},"3":{"en":"Maudlin"},"4":{"en":"Sardonic"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Lugubrious (शोकपूर्ण, उदास) = looking or sounding sad and dismal.</b><br><b>Jubilant (आनंदित)</b> = extremely happy; the option also misspells it as “jubiliant.”<br><b>Maudlin (भावुकतापूर्ण)</b> = excessively sentimental<br><b>Sardonic (व्यंग्यपूर्ण)</b> = grimly mocking or cynical<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Lugubrious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074568","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Select the correct option:<br>The sociologist was renowned for her ___ analysis of systemic inequalities. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"penetrative"},"2":{"en":"penetrating"},"3":{"en":"penetrable"},"4":{"en":"penetrated"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Penetrating (सूक्ष्म और गहन) = showing deep understanding and insight.</b><br>The adjective “penetrating” naturally describes an insightful analysis.<br>“Penetrative” refers chiefly to physical entry; “penetrable” means capable of being entered.<br>“Penetrated” is a past participle and is not idiomatic before “analysis.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): penetrating.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074569","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The editor-in-chief asked whether (1)/ the article had underwent (2)/ plagiarism screening (3)/ before approval. (4) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: After “had,” use the past participle “undergone.”</b><br>“Underwent” is the simple past, so part (2) is erroneous.<br>Correct phrase: “the article <b>had undergone</b> plagiarism screening.”<br>The other parts contain no grammatical error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074570","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The tribunal objected to not the content of the testimony (1)/ but the manner in which it was introduced (2)/ without any authentication by the official registrar (3)/ or acknowledgment of its provenance. (4) [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In the correlative structure “not … but,” “not” must precede the object directly.</b><br>Part (1) should read “The tribunal objected <b>not to</b> the content of the testimony.”<br>The contrast is then correctly completed by “but the manner ….”<br>Parts (2), (3) and (4) are structurally sound.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074571","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>We must obey the rules. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The rules must be obeyed."},"2":{"en":"The rules must have been obeyed."},"3":{"en":"The rules had to be obeyed."},"4":{"en":"The rules are being obeyed."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Modal passive = modal + be + past participle.</b><br>“The rules” becomes the subject, while “must” remains unchanged.<br>Correct form: “The rules <b>must be obeyed</b>.”<br>B changes the aspect, C changes the modal force, and D uses present continuous passive.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The rules must be obeyed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074572","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They should not have let misinformation spread unchecked. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Misinformation should not have let to spread unchecked."},"2":{"en":"Misinformation should not be spread unchecked."},"3":{"en":"Misinformation should not have been allowed to spread unchecked."},"4":{"en":"Misinformation should not have spread unchecked."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Let + object + base verb” becomes “object + be allowed to + base verb.”</b><br>The perfect modal is retained: “should not have been allowed.”<br>A incorrectly keeps “let”; B loses the perfect meaning.<br>D removes the idea of permission and changes the causative structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Misinformation should not have been allowed to spread unchecked.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074573","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>He said that he would rather have been punished than be humiliated publicly. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“I would rather be punished than get humiliated publicly,” he said."},"2":{"en":"“I would rather have been punished than be humiliated publicly,” he said."},"3":{"en":"“I prefer punishment over humiliation,” he said."},"4":{"en":"“I'd rather punishment than public humiliation,” he said."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Change the reported third person to “I” and preserve the perfect infinitive.</b><br>The original preference concerns a completed alternative: “would rather have been punished.”<br>A changes the perfect infinitive; C paraphrases the structure.<br>D omits the verb “be” and does not preserve the original construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): “I would rather have been punished than be humiliated publicly,” he said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074574","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.<br>Fame can be <u>ephemeral</u> if not sustained by talent. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Permanent"},"2":{"en":"Temporary"},"3":{"en":"Lasting"},"4":{"en":"Constant"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Ephemeral (क्षणभंगुर) = lasting for a very short time.</b><br><b>Permanent (स्थायी)</b> = lasting indefinitely<br><b>Temporary (अस्थायी)</b> = lasting for a limited time ✔<br><b>Lasting (टिकाऊ)</b> = enduring over time<br><b>Constant (निरंतर)</b> = unchanging or continuous<br>More synonyms: fleeting, transient, short-lived.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Temporary.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074575","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named A, B, C, and D. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. The global fashion industry<br>A. shifting toward sustainable fabrics<br>B. is undergoing a transformation<br>C. to reduce their massive<br>D. as more brands are<br>6. environmental footprint and waste. [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BDAC"},"2":{"en":"DCAB"},"3":{"en":"ACBD"},"4":{"en":"BACD"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: BDAC</b><br>B supplies the main predicate “is undergoing a transformation.”<br>D introduces the reason, and A completes it: brands are shifting towards sustainable fabrics.<br>C joins part 6 to state the goal: reducing their environmental footprint and waste.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): BDAC.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074576","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>High above the city, on a tall column, stood the statue of the Happy Prince. The statue was covered with thin leaves of fine gold. It had two bright sapphires for eyes, and a large red ruby shone on the hilt of its sword.<br><br>The people of the city greatly admired the statue. “It is as beautiful as a weathercock,” remarked a Town Councillor who wished to be known for his artistic taste. “However, it is not quite as useful,” he added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.<br><br>A sensible mother pointed towards the statue and said to her little boy, who was crying for the moon, “Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”<br><br>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man as he looked at the magnificent statue.<br><br>The Charity Children, dressed in bright scarlet cloaks and clean white pinafores, saw the statue while leaving the cathedral. “The Happy Prince looks just like an angel,” they said.<br><br>“How do you know what an angel looks like?” asked the Mathematical Master. “You have never seen one.”<br><br>“We have seen angels in our dreams,” replied the children. The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.<br><br>One night, a little Swallow flew over the city. His friends had already left for Egypt, but he had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed. He had met the Reed in the spring while chasing a yellow moth along the river and stopped to speak to her.<br><br><br>Why did the Town Councillor add that the statue was “not quite as useful” as a weathercock? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He feared that people might regard him as an impractical person."},"2":{"en":"He believed that public statues should always serve a practical purpose."},"3":{"en":"He considered the statue less attractive than an ordinary weathercock."},"4":{"en":"He wanted the statue to be removed from the tall column."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Reason: He wanted to protect his reputation for practicality.</b><br><i>“He added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.”</i><br>This directly explains his qualification.<br>He does not demand usefulness from every statue, call it less attractive, or seek its removal.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): He feared that people might regard him as an impractical person.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074577","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>High above the city, on a tall column, stood the statue of the Happy Prince. The statue was covered with thin leaves of fine gold. It had two bright sapphires for eyes, and a large red ruby shone on the hilt of its sword.<br><br>The people of the city greatly admired the statue. “It is as beautiful as a weathercock,” remarked a Town Councillor who wished to be known for his artistic taste. “However, it is not quite as useful,” he added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.<br><br>A sensible mother pointed towards the statue and said to her little boy, who was crying for the moon, “Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”<br><br>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man as he looked at the magnificent statue.<br><br>The Charity Children, dressed in bright scarlet cloaks and clean white pinafores, saw the statue while leaving the cathedral. “The Happy Prince looks just like an angel,” they said.<br><br>“How do you know what an angel looks like?” asked the Mathematical Master. “You have never seen one.”<br><br>“We have seen angels in our dreams,” replied the children. The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.<br><br>One night, a little Swallow flew over the city. His friends had already left for Egypt, but he had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed. He had met the Reed in the spring while chasing a yellow moth along the river and stopped to speak to her.<br><br><br>What does the disappointed man’s remark about the Happy Prince reveal? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He believed that the Prince had overcome every personal difficulty."},"2":{"en":"He wished to possess the wealth displayed upon the golden statue."},"3":{"en":"He assumed that the Prince represented happiness absent from his own life."},"4":{"en":"He doubted whether complete happiness could exist anywhere in the world."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>The remark contrasts another’s apparent happiness with his own disappointment.</b><br><i>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man.</i><br>He therefore assumes the Prince possesses the happiness he lacks.<br>No personal struggle, desire for the statue’s wealth, or general disbelief in happiness is stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He assumed that the Prince represented happiness absent from his own life.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074578","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>High above the city, on a tall column, stood the statue of the Happy Prince. The statue was covered with thin leaves of fine gold. It had two bright sapphires for eyes, and a large red ruby shone on the hilt of its sword.<br><br>The people of the city greatly admired the statue. “It is as beautiful as a weathercock,” remarked a Town Councillor who wished to be known for his artistic taste. “However, it is not quite as useful,” he added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.<br><br>A sensible mother pointed towards the statue and said to her little boy, who was crying for the moon, “Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”<br><br>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man as he looked at the magnificent statue.<br><br>The Charity Children, dressed in bright scarlet cloaks and clean white pinafores, saw the statue while leaving the cathedral. “The Happy Prince looks just like an angel,” they said.<br><br>“How do you know what an angel looks like?” asked the Mathematical Master. “You have never seen one.”<br><br>“We have seen angels in our dreams,” replied the children. The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.<br><br>One night, a little Swallow flew over the city. His friends had already left for Egypt, but he had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed. He had met the Reed in the spring while chasing a yellow moth along the river and stopped to speak to her.<br><br><br>Why did the Mathematical Master frown at the Charity Children’s reply? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He thought that their comparison of the statue with an angel was disrespectful."},"2":{"en":"He believed that children should describe only what they saw in the cathedral."},"3":{"en":"He suspected that the children were inventing stories to impress their teacher."},"4":{"en":"He disapproved of children accepting dreams as a source of knowledge."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Reason: He rejected dreaming as a valid activity or source of knowledge.</b><br><i>“The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.”</i><br>The children had cited angels seen in dreams, which explains his response.<br>Disrespect, cathedral-only description and deliberate invention are not suggested.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): He disapproved of children accepting dreams as a source of knowledge.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074579","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>High above the city, on a tall column, stood the statue of the Happy Prince. The statue was covered with thin leaves of fine gold. It had two bright sapphires for eyes, and a large red ruby shone on the hilt of its sword.<br><br>The people of the city greatly admired the statue. “It is as beautiful as a weathercock,” remarked a Town Councillor who wished to be known for his artistic taste. “However, it is not quite as useful,” he added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.<br><br>A sensible mother pointed towards the statue and said to her little boy, who was crying for the moon, “Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”<br><br>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man as he looked at the magnificent statue.<br><br>The Charity Children, dressed in bright scarlet cloaks and clean white pinafores, saw the statue while leaving the cathedral. “The Happy Prince looks just like an angel,” they said.<br><br>“How do you know what an angel looks like?” asked the Mathematical Master. “You have never seen one.”<br><br>“We have seen angels in our dreams,” replied the children. The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.<br><br>One night, a little Swallow flew over the city. His friends had already left for Egypt, but he had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed. He had met the Reed in the spring while chasing a yellow moth along the river and stopped to speak to her.<br><br><br>Which of the following best describes the irony in the mother’s statement to her child? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She expects a young child to understand the artistic value of a golden statue."},"2":{"en":"She holds up an unfeeling, inanimate object as a model of perfect emotional behaviour."},"3":{"en":"She praises the Prince’s behaviour while ignoring his immense material wealth."},"4":{"en":"She scolds her child for crying while she herself is acting impatiently."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Irony: A lifeless statue is presented as a model for controlling human emotion.</b><br><i>“Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”</i><br>The statue cannot feel or cry, making the comparison emotionally unreasonable.<br>Artistic appreciation, material wealth and the mother’s impatience are not the central irony.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She holds up an unfeeling, inanimate object as a model of perfect emotional behaviour.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074580","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>High above the city, on a tall column, stood the statue of the Happy Prince. The statue was covered with thin leaves of fine gold. It had two bright sapphires for eyes, and a large red ruby shone on the hilt of its sword.<br><br>The people of the city greatly admired the statue. “It is as beautiful as a weathercock,” remarked a Town Councillor who wished to be known for his artistic taste. “However, it is not quite as useful,” he added, fearing that others might consider him impractical.<br><br>A sensible mother pointed towards the statue and said to her little boy, who was crying for the moon, “Why can’t you behave like the Happy Prince? The Happy Prince never cries for anything.”<br><br>“I am glad that someone in the world is completely happy,” muttered a disappointed man as he looked at the magnificent statue.<br><br>The Charity Children, dressed in bright scarlet cloaks and clean white pinafores, saw the statue while leaving the cathedral. “The Happy Prince looks just like an angel,” they said.<br><br>“How do you know what an angel looks like?” asked the Mathematical Master. “You have never seen one.”<br><br>“We have seen angels in our dreams,” replied the children. The Mathematical Master frowned because he did not approve of children dreaming.<br><br>One night, a little Swallow flew over the city. His friends had already left for Egypt, but he had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed. He had met the Reed in the spring while chasing a yellow moth along the river and stopped to speak to her.<br><br><br>Which inference can most reasonably be drawn from the Swallow's decision to remain behind? [SSC CGL 08/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He had been separated from his companions while searching for food near the river."},"2":{"en":"He intended to remain in the city permanently because he disliked travelling to Egypt."},"3":{"en":"His pursuit of the yellow moth prevented him from learning when his friends departed."},"4":{"en":"His emotional attachment caused him to postpone joining his friends on their journey."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Inference: Love delayed his migration.</b><br><i>“He had stayed behind because he was in love with a beautiful Reed.”</i><br>His attachment to the Reed made him postpone joining his friends in Egypt.<br>The passage does not mention searching for food, permanent residence, dislike of Egypt, or ignorance of their departure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): His emotional attachment caused him to postpone joining his friends on their journey.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};